---@field id string The unique identifier of the access point.
---@field name string The human-readable name of the access point. Must be unique per share.
---@field share_id string The unique identifier of the share this access point belongs to.
---@field path string The export sub-path for this access point (always starts with `/`).
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.AccessPointResponseStatus The current lifecycle status of an access point. There is no ACCESS_POINT_DELETING state: DELETE soft-deletes the access point synchronously (mirroring share deletion); the response of a delete request returns the access point already in ACCESS_POINT_DELETED.
---@field access_policy digitalocean.digitalocean.AccessPolicy
---@field created_at string The timestamp when the access point was created.
---@field updated_at string The timestamp when the access point was last updated. May be empty while the access point is still being created.
---@field is_default boolean Whether this is the share's default access point.
---@field vpc_id? string The VPC this access point is pinned to. Omitted on the default access point. Every non-default access point owns its own storage gateway in this VPC and is independent of the parent share's VPC lifecycle.

---The current lifecycle status of an access point. There is no ACCESS_POINT_DELETING state:
---DELETE soft-deletes the access point synchronously (mirroring share deletion);
