---AgentKind identifies what runs inside the session sandbox. CreateSession accepts CLAUDE_CODE, OPENCODE, CODEX_CLI, CURSOR_CLI, OPENAI_CODEX, LANGGRAPH, and CREWAI (the supported set is overridable via HARNESS_SUPPORTED_AGENT_KINDS); other values are rejected with 400. AGENT_KIND_OPENAI_CODEX is the OpenAI sandbox-provider kind (DO runs codex exec-server; the agent loop lives at OpenAI). AGENT_KIND_LANGGRAPH is the LangGraph framework adapter. AGENT_KIND_CREWAI is the CrewAI Crew framework adapter: like LANGGRAPH the template bakes no agent code, so spec.env must supply FRAMEWORK_REPO and FRAMEWORK_REPO_SHA; a Crew kickoff is one-shot and exposes no HITL surface. CREWAI is additionally gated per team and returns 400 for teams it is not enabled for.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentKind "AGENT_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"AGENT_KIND_CLAUDE_CODE"|"AGENT_KIND_OPENCODE"|"AGENT_KIND_CODEX_CLI"|"AGENT_KIND_CURSOR_CLI"|"AGENT_KIND_NONE"|"AGENT_KIND_CUSTOM"|"AGENT_KIND_HERMES"|"AGENT_KIND_OPENAI_CODEX"|"AGENT_KIND_LANGGRAPH"|"AGENT_KIND_CREWAI"

---Customer-authored agents.yaml Agent manifest, sent as the CreateSession request body with a YAML Content-Type. Two formats are accepted during the dual-format transition: the FLAT format (primary - no envelope, snake_case, duration strings; authoritative published schema contracts/agent.flat.schema.json, field reference docs/agent-manifest.md) and the legacy v1alpha1 envelope documented by the properties below (DEPRECATED; schema contracts/agent.v1alpha1.schema.json; parses append a deprecation notice to session.warnings). A top-level apiVersion key selects the legacy parser; its absence selects flat. Untrusted input: every value is a request that is validated and clamped server-side. Decoding is strict in both formats: unknown or misspelled fields are rejected with HTTP 400 (with did-you-mean and legacy-spelling hints on the flat path).
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifest
---@field apiVersion? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestApiVersion Legacy envelope only - must be "agents.digitalocean.com/v1alpha1", and its presence is what routes the document to the deprecated legacy parser. Flat-format manifests carry no version key (the endpoint owns the contract); required, with kind and spec, when authoring the legacy format.
---@field kind? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestKind Must be "Agent".
---@field metadata? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestMetadata
---@field spec? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpec

---Legacy envelope only - must be "agents.digitalocean.com/v1alpha1", and its presence is what routes the document to the deprecated legacy parser. Flat-format manifests carry no version key (the endpoint owns the contract); required, with kind and spec, when authoring the legacy format.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestApiVersion "agents.digitalocean.com/v1alpha1"

---Must be "Agent".
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestKind "Agent"

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestMetadata
---@field name? string Optional team-unique session name: 1-64 chars of letters, digits, '-', '.', '_', starting and ending alphanumeric; case-insensitive; must not be UUID-shaped. Omit to have the control plane generate one ("session-<agent-type>-<date-time>"). Unique among the team's ACTIVE (non-terminal) sessions; destroying a session frees its name for reuse.
---@field description? string Free-form description (max 1024 chars), stored and echoed back for Console / catalog surfaces.
---@field labels? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestMetadataLabelsMap

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestMetadataLabelsMap { [string]: string }

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpec
---@field permissions? digitalocean.digitalocean.Permissions
---@field mode? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecMode Explicit lifecycle discriminator. Defaults to "interactive" (spec.serving forbidden); "served" requires spec.serving.
---@field runtime digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecRuntime Canonical adapter ids: claude-code | opencode | codex | cursor | hermes | codex-agentapi | custom. codex-agentapi is the OpenAI sandbox-provider runtime (DO runs codex exec-server; the agent loop lives at OpenAI) and pairs with the opaque spec.runtime.config block. codex-cli and cursor-cli are deprecated aliases (accepted with a create-time warning). The framework adapters (openai-agents, claude-agent-sdk, crewai, langgraph) are declared but not yet supported; CreateSession rejects them. adapter: custom requires the custom block.
---@field workspace? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecWorkspace Repositories the session works against.
---@field sandbox? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandbox
---@field model? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecModel Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). Model routing (Plano); catalog-validated when enforcement lands.
---@field tools? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecTools Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). Exactly one of mcpServers or bundle.
---@field skills? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSkillsList Inline agent skills (SKILL.md shape): reusable markdown instructions the agent loads on demand, selected by description. Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). Max 32 entries; instructions additionally capped at 256 KiB summed across the list so a valid manifest always fits the request-body limits. v0 is inline-only - remote skill sources come later as an additive field.
---@field env? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecEnvMap Non-secret guest env (debug-readable - never put secrets here; use spec.secrets). Reserved platform keys (TEAM_ID, SESSION_ID, SANDBOX_ID, CONTROL_PLANE_CALLBACK_URL, SANDBOX_TEMPLATE, SANDBOX_AGENT_WORKDIR, SIZE_SLUG, SANDBOX_IMAGE_ID, SANDBOX_OCI_REF, PLANO_PERMISSION_*) are rejected. Credential-looking values (dop_v1_..., sk-..., ghp_...) trigger a create-time warning.
---@field memory? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecMemory Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning).
---@field secrets? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSecretsList Declared credential requirements. source tenantSecret is enforced today: value is write-only plaintext, extracted into Secrets Manager at create and never persisted or returned. source oauth requires provider, carries no value, and is accepted but not yet enforced. ref is legacy and ignored. env false keeps the resolved value out of the guest environment (mount-only slots).
---@field defaults? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecDefaults
---@field serving? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecServing Present only when spec.mode is "served" (autoscaled fleet).

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecDefaults
---@field budget? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecDefaultsBudget Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). Advisory per-run ceilings, clamped server-side to tenant policy.

---Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). Advisory per-run ceilings, clamped server-side to tenant policy.
