---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandbox
---@field template? string Optional sandbox template. Empty (or the legacy placeholder "coding") means "no preference": the template derives from the adapter.
---@field persistentWorkspace? boolean
---@field idleTimeoutSeconds? number Inactivity suspend timeout. 0 means tenant policy default.
---@field maxLifetimeSeconds? number Hard wall-clock ceiling for the whole session, independent of activity. Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning).
---@field sizeSlug? string Requested sandbox size (catalog: GET /v2/agents/sessions/sandbox/sizes). Empty means the service default.
---@field mounts? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandboxMountsList Requested data mounts. Accepted, not yet enforced (returns a warning). accessKeyRef/secretKeyRef name declared tenantSecret slots in spec.secrets, validated at create; declare those slots with env: false so the keys stay mount-scoped and out of the guest env.
---@field egress? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandboxEgress Requested egress policy (legacy envelope object). Absent means no destination ACL, same as unrestricted: true. unrestricted cannot combine with allow / allowIps / vpcUuid / subnetUuid. If allow or allowIps is present and neither list names an entry, the policy is deny-all: every outbound destination is blocked. Deny-all cannot combine with unrestricted / vpcUuid / subnetUuid, and a session that also binds URL-bound credentials is rejected with 400. If the other list names entries, only those are allowed (allow: [] with a non-empty allowIps is IP-only). A null egress, allow or allowIps is rejected with 400; omit the key instead. The flat manifest format spells these differently: egress: none (deny-all), egress: unrestricted, a bare host list (an empty list is deny-all), or an object with allow_hosts / allow_ips / vpc_uuid / subnet_uuid. Platform host defaults are unioned only when allow names something; allowIps does not trigger that union (IP-only turns the destination ACL on without domain rules). VPC attachment is create-time immutable; ownership is verified at session create. Allowlists are a request only: the server intersects them with tenant + platform policy and can only narrow them.

---Requested egress policy (legacy envelope object). Absent means no destination ACL, same as unrestricted: true. unrestricted cannot combine with allow / allowIps / vpcUuid / subnetUuid. If allow or allowIps is present and neither list names an entry, the policy is deny-all: every outbound destination is blocked. Deny-all cannot combine with unrestricted / vpcUuid / subnetUuid, and a session that also binds URL-bound credentials is rejected with 400. If the other list names entries, only those are allowed (allow: [] with a non-empty allowIps is IP-only). A null egress, allow or allowIps is rejected with 400; omit the key instead. The flat manifest format spells these differently: egress: none (deny-all), egress: unrestricted, a bare host list (an empty list is deny-all), or an object with allow_hosts / allow_ips / vpc_uuid / subnet_uuid. Platform host defaults are unioned only when allow names something; allowIps does not trigger that union (IP-only turns the destination ACL on without domain rules). VPC attachment is create-time immutable; ownership is verified at session create. Allowlists are a request only: the server intersects them with tenant + platform policy and can only narrow them.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandboxEgress
---@field allow? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandboxEgressAllowList Host allowlist. allow: [] with no non-empty allowIps means deny-all (flat spelling: egress: none). With a non-empty allowIps it is IP-only.
---@field allowIps? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecSandboxEgressAllowIpsList Exact IPv4/IPv6 literals (not CIDRs). Present-but-empty with no non-empty allow means deny-all; allow: [] with a non-empty allowIps is IP-only.
---@field vpcUuid? string Customer VPC UUID. Create-time immutable.
---@field subnetUuid? string Optional subnet within vpcUuid.
---@field unrestricted? boolean When true, opts out of the platform-default host allowlist union. Mutually exclusive with allow / allowIps / vpcUuid / subnetUuid.

