---@field name? string Inline server name (required with url): 1-64 chars of lowercase letters, digits, '-', '.', '_', starting/ending alphanumeric. Unique across the list. Must not start with do. (reserved for catalog refs).
---@field url? string Inline server endpoint; https:// only.
---@field tools? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecToolsMcpServersItemToolsList Optional selection allowlist; omitted means all tools the server advertises. Each entry is an individual tool name with an optional integer version pin (e.g. web_search, execute_code@3) or a toolbelt reference - a server-defined named tool group written toolbelt:<name>[@<int>] (e.g. toolbelt:read-only@1; catalog refs only). Versions are integer pins (no semver). The server owns belt expansion; a pinned tool or belt attaches exactly that version, an unpinned one resolves at session create and is frozen for the session (no floating latest). Entries non-empty, unique per server. The selection bounds the session and is never preloaded into the session MCP tools/list; see preloadTools.
---@field preloadTools? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecToolsMcpServersItemPreloadToolsList Catalog form only. Individual tools (optional integer pin) advertised directly in the session MCP tools/list next to the action_search/action_invoke/action_code meta tools. Each entry must appear in tools when tools is set; toolbelt references are rejected. Every preloaded schema is in the model's context on every turn, so keep this to a handful of tools. Omitted means nothing is preloaded.
---@field auth? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentManifestSpecToolsMcpServersItemAuth Brokered credential for an INLINE server (invalid on the catalog form). secretRef names a declared tenantSecret slot in spec.secrets, validated at create; the slot is resolved server-side and sent as an HTTP header. Plaintext credentials are never accepted.

