---Whether a catalog row is a foundation model or an Inference Router preset.
---
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_MODEL: A foundation or inference model.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_INFERENCE_ROUTER: An Inference Router preset.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ApiModelCatalogItemType "MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_MODEL"|"MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_INFERENCE_ROUTER"

---Compact canary performance rollup for catalog browse and the catalog card.
---List Model Catalog V2 uses a rolling last-24-hour window (window_days is 1).
---Get Model Catalog Card V2 uses the sample-weighted mean of daily percentiles
---over the liveliness window, typically 7 days. The full daily series stays on
---liveliness. This is canary traffic, not live customer load.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ApiModelCatalogPerformance
---@field e2e_latency_p50_seconds? number End-to-end latency in seconds, p50.
---@field e2e_latency_p75_seconds? number End-to-end latency in seconds, p75.
---@field e2e_latency_p95_seconds? number End-to-end latency in seconds, p95.
---@field samples? number Request samples across the window. Prefers end-to-end latency, then time to first token, then throughput.
---@field status? string "ok" when time to first token, end-to-end latency, and throughput all have data, "partial_data" when only some do, "insufficient_data" when none do.
---@field throughput_p50_tok_per_s? number Throughput in tokens per second, p50.
---@field throughput_p75_tok_per_s? number Throughput in tokens per second, p75.
---@field throughput_p95_tok_per_s? number Throughput in tokens per second, p95.
---@field ttft_p50_seconds? number Time to first token in seconds, p50. Streaming canary probes only.
---@field ttft_p75_seconds? number Time to first token in seconds, p75. Streaming canary probes only.
---@field ttft_p95_seconds? number Time to first token in seconds, p95. Streaming canary probes only.
---@field window_days? number Lookback window length in days. 1 is the rolling 24-hour list window.

---Product that offers the model. Serving (serverless or dedicated) is separate.
---
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATIONS_JUDGE: Model can judge evaluations.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_HARNESS_RUNTIME: Model is enrolled for the harness runtime.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATION_CANDIDATE: Model can be an evaluation or simulation candidate.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ApiModelCatalogProduct "MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_UNSPECIFIED"|"MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATIONS_JUDGE"|"MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_HARNESS_RUNTIME"|"MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATION_CANDIDATE"

---Field on which to sort model catalog results.
---
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT: Default: sort by creation date.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_NAME: Sort by the model's display name (case-insensitive).
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_PRICE: Sort by input token price.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ApiModelCatalogSortBy "MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_NAME"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_PRICE"

---Field on which to sort V2 model catalog results.
---
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT: Default: sort by creation date.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_NAME: Sort by the model's display name (case-insensitive).
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_PRICE: Sort by input token price.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_E2E_LATENCY_P50: Sort by canary end-to-end latency p50, in seconds. Lower is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_THROUGHPUT_P50: Sort by canary throughput p50, in tokens per second. Higher is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data.
--- - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_TTFT_P50: Sort by canary time to first token p50, in seconds. Lower is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ApiModelCatalogSortByV2 "MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_NAME"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_PRICE"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_E2E_LATENCY_P50"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_THROUGHPUT_P50"|"MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_TTFT_P50"

