---@field rules? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRulesList Rules for configuring HTTP ingress for component routes, CORS, rewrites, and redirects.
---@field custom_error_page_url? string Optional HTTPS URL of a custom error page to display when the app is unreachable. The page is shown in a full-viewport iframe. The target must allow framing: avoid `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and a restrictive `Content-Security-Policy` `frame-ancestors` that blocks the platform. If omitted, the default platform error page is used.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRule
---@field match? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleMatch
---@field cors? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppsCorsPolicy
---@field component? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleRoutingComponent
---@field redirect? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleRoutingRedirect

---The match configuration for the rule.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleMatch
---@field path? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleStringMatchPrefix
---@field authority? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleStringMatchExact

---The component to route to. Only one of `component` or `redirect` may be set.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleRoutingComponent
---@field name string The name of the component to route to.
---@field preserve_path_prefix? string An optional flag to preserve the path that is forwarded to the backend service. By default, the HTTP request path will be trimmed from the left when forwarded to the component. For example, a component with `path=/api` will have requests to `/api/list` trimmed to `/list`. If this value is `true`, the path will remain `/api/list`. Note: this is not applicable for Functions Components and is mutually exclusive with `rewrite`.
---@field rewrite? string An optional field that will rewrite the path of the component to be what is specified here. By default, the HTTP request path will be trimmed from the left when forwarded to the component. For example, a component with `path=/api` will have requests to `/api/list` trimmed to `/list`. If you specified the rewrite to be `/v1/`, requests to `/api/list` would be rewritten to `/v1/list`. Note: this is mutually exclusive with `preserve_path_prefix`.

---The redirect configuration for the rule. Only one of `component` or `redirect` may be set.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleRoutingRedirect
---@field uri? string An optional URI path to redirect to. Note: if this is specified the whole URI of the original request will be overwritten to this value, irrespective of the original request URI being matched.
---@field authority? string The authority/host to redirect to. This can be a hostname or IP address. Note: use `port` to set the port.
---@field port? number The port to redirect to.
---@field scheme? string The scheme to redirect to. Supported values are `http` or `https`. Default: `https`.
---@field redirect_code? number The redirect code to use. Defaults to `302`. Supported values are 300, 301, 302, 303, 304, 307, 308.

---The authority to match on.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleStringMatchExact
---@field exact string|distilled.Null Exact string match. An empty string is a valid value and will be serialized explicitly rather than being omitted from the payload.

---The path to match on.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRuleStringMatchPrefix
---@field prefix string|distilled.Null Prefix-based match. For example, `/api` will match `/api`, `/api/`, and any nested paths such as `/api/v1/endpoint`.

---Rules for configuring HTTP ingress for component routes, CORS, rewrites, and redirects.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRulesList digitalocean.digitalocean.AppIngressSpecRule[]

