---The desired configuration of an application.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AppSpec
---@field name string The name of the app. Must be unique across all apps in the same account.
---@field region? digitalocean.digitalocean.AppSpecRegion The slug form of the geographical origin of the app. Default: `nearest available`
---@field disable_edge_cache? boolean If set to `true`, the app will **not** be cached at the edge (CDN). Enable this option if you want to manage CDN configuration yourself—whether by using an external CDN provider or by handling static content and caching within your app. This setting is also recommended for apps that require real-time data or serve dynamic content, such as those using Server-Sent Events (SSE) over GET, or hosting an MCP (Model Context Protocol) Server that utilizes SSE. **Note:** This feature is not available for static site components. For more information, see [Disable CDN Cache](https://docs.digitalocean.com/products/app-platform/how-to/cache-content/#disable-cdn-cache).
---@field disable_email_obfuscation? boolean If set to `true`, email addresses in the app will not be obfuscated. This is useful for apps that require email addresses to be visible (in the HTML markup).
---@field enhanced_threat_control_enabled? boolean If set to `true`, suspicious requests will go through additional security checks to help mitigate layer 7 DDoS attacks.
