---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.AutoscalePoolDropletTemplate
---@field name? string The name(s) to be applied to all Droplets in the autoscale pool.
---@field region digitalocean.digitalocean.AutoscalePoolDropletTemplateRegion|string The datacenter in which all of the Droplets will be created.
---@field size string The Droplet size to be used for all Droplets in the autoscale pool.
---@field image string The Droplet image to be used for all Droplets in the autoscale pool. You may specify the slug or the image ID.
---@field ssh_keys digitalocean.digitalocean.AutoscalePoolDropletTemplateSshKeysList The SSH keys to be installed on the Droplets in the autoscale pool. You can either specify the key ID or the fingerprint. Requires `ssh_key:read` scope.
---@field tags? digitalocean.digitalocean.AutoscalePoolDropletTemplateTagsList The tags to apply to each of the Droplets in the autoscale pool. Requires `tag:read` scope.
---@field vpc_uuid? string The VPC where the Droplets in the autoscale pool will be created. The VPC must be in the region where you want to create the Droplets. Requires `vpc:read` scope.
---@field with_droplet_agent? boolean Installs the Droplet agent. This must be set to true to monitor Droplets for resource utilization scaling.
---@field project_id? string The project that the Droplets in the autoscale pool will belong to. Requires `project:read` scope.
---@field ipv6? boolean Assigns a unique IPv6 address to each of the Droplets in the autoscale pool.
---@field user_data? string A string containing user data that cloud-init consumes to configure a Droplet on first boot. User data is often a cloud-config file or Bash script. It must be plain text and may not exceed 64 KiB in size.
---@field public_networking? boolean An optional boolean indicating whether the Droplets should be created with public networking or not. By default, all Droplets are created with public networking available. If explicitly set to `false`, only private networking will be enabled, and public networking will be disabled; currently this means that it will not have any public static or Reserved IPv4 or IPv6 address, nor can one be assigned later. If explicitly set to `false`, `ipv6` must also be `false`.

