---Present when this tool accepts cache controls in the session. Unlike the catalog's cache.ttlSeconds, this describes the session's caching opt-in.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheAdvertisement
---@field maxAgeSeconds number Maximum result age the session allows, or 300 if the session sets no limit. The tool's own cache lifetime can be shorter. Invoke controls use max_age_seconds, not this field's camelCase spelling.

---Optional per-call caching controls. Send beside arguments, not inside them. Accepted only for tools opted into caching in this session; tool search advertises these tools with a cache field. Omitting controls uses the session's settings. Direct MCP tools/call requests use session settings without overrides; use action_invoke for per-call controls.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheControls
---@field mode? digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheControlsMode|string auto uses a sufficiently recent cached result or calls the provider and can store a successful result. bypass skips lookup and storage without clearing or refreshing existing entries.
---@field max_age_seconds? number Oldest cached result this call accepts, in seconds. Zero bypasses caching. Values above 300 are clamped to 300; larger values cannot increase the session or tool lifetime. This controls accepted result age, not the lifetime of a newly stored entry.

---auto uses a sufficiently recent cached result or calls the provider and can store a successful result. bypass skips lookup and storage without clearing or refreshing existing entries.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheControlsMode "auto"|"bypass"

---Cache outcome. Hits always include this metadata. MISS and BYPASS appear only when the call includes cache controls. Cache hits still incur the gateway invocation charge but not an additional provider charge.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheStatus
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheStatusStatus HIT returned a cached result without calling the provider. MISS found no usable result and called the provider. BYPASS skipped caching.
---@field age_seconds? number Age of the cached result in seconds. Present only on a hit.

---HIT returned a cached result without calling the provider. MISS found no usable result and called the provider. BYPASS skipped caching.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CacheStatusStatus "HIT"|"MISS"|"BYPASS"

