---The type of health check to perform.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CheckType "ping"|"http"|"https"

---Checkpoint is a durable capture of a session's live sandbox machine state bound to the event-log cursor at the cut. READY checkpoints seed forks (ForkSession) and rollback. Internal fields (team_id, the substrate checkpoint id, event_seq) are never serialized.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Checkpoint
---@field checkpoint_id? string Public checkpoint id, stable for the checkpoint's lifetime (e.g. cp_9f2c1a4b).
---@field session_id? string Owning session.
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.CheckpointStatus
---@field kind? digitalocean.digitalocean.CheckpointKind
---@field label? string Optional user-supplied label from CreateCheckpoint; empty when omitted.
---@field event_id? string Event-log cursor (ULID) of the last event included in the cut; forks resume event replay from here.
---@field size_bytes? number Size of the captured machine state. 0 until the checkpoint reaches READY.
---@field created_at? string
---@field error_message? string Client-safe failure detail; set only when status is FAILED.

---A checkpoint of a MicroVM's memory and disk. New MicroVMs created from a checkpoint start from that state.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Checkpoint2
---@field id string The unique ID of the checkpoint.
---@field name? string The name of the checkpoint. If you do not set one, a name such as `checkpoint-20260929-143559` is generated.
---@field microvm_id? string The ID of the MicroVM the checkpoint was taken from.
---@field microvm_name? string The name of the MicroVM the checkpoint was taken from.
---@field region? string The slug of the checkpoint's region.
---@field size? digitalocean.digitalocean.MicrovmSize
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.Checkpoint2Status The checkpoint's status. You can create MicroVMs from the checkpoint when it is `CHECKPOINT_AVAILABLE`.
---@field failure_reason? string Why the checkpoint failed. Present only when `status` is `CHECKPOINT_FAILED`.
---@field egress_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.MicrovmEgressPolicy
---@field memory_bytes? number The stored size of the checkpoint's memory, in bytes.
---@field disk_bytes? number The stored size of the checkpoint's disk, in bytes.
---@field created_at string When the checkpoint was created, in ISO 8601 format.

---The checkpoint's status. You can create MicroVMs from the checkpoint when it is `CHECKPOINT_AVAILABLE`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.Checkpoint2Status "CHECKPOINT_CREATING"|"CHECKPOINT_AVAILABLE"|"CHECKPOINT_FAILED"|"CHECKPOINT_DELETING"|"CHECKPOINT_DELETED"

---How the checkpoint came to exist: explicit - requested via CreateCheckpoint; implicit - minted automatically by the platform (on run completion, or when ForkSession is called without from_checkpoint_id).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CheckpointKind "explicit"|"implicit"

---Capture lifecycle: PENDING -> READY | FAILED. Only READY checkpoints are forkable/restorable. CreateCheckpoint blocks until terminal, so PENDING is only ever observable via list/get while a capture is in flight.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CheckpointStatus "PENDING"|"READY"|"FAILED"

---An object specifying custom cluster autoscaler configuration.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfiguration
---@field scale_down_utilization_threshold? number Used to customize when cluster autoscaler scales down non-empty nodes by setting the node utilization threshold.
---@field scale_down_unneeded_time? string Used to customize how long a node is unneeded before being scaled down.
---@field expanders? digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfigurationExpandersList Customizes expanders used by cluster-autoscaler. The autoscaler will apply each expander from the provided list to narrow down the selection of node types created to scale up, until either a single node type is left, or the list of expanders is exhausted. If this flag is unset, autoscaler will use its default expander `random`. Passing an empty list (_not_ `null`) will unset any previous expander customizations. Available expanders: - `random`: Randomly selects a node group to scale. - `priority`: Selects the node group with the highest priority as per [user-provided configuration](https://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/how-to/autoscale/#configuring-priority-expander) - `least_waste`: Selects the node group that will result in the least amount of idle resources.

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfigurationExpandersItem "random"|"priority"|"least_waste"

---Customizes expanders used by cluster-autoscaler.
---The autoscaler will apply each expander from the provided list to narrow down the selection of node types created to scale up,
---until either a single node type is left, or the list of expanders is exhausted.
---If this flag is unset, autoscaler will use its default expander `random`.
---Passing an empty list (_not_ `null`) will unset any previous expander customizations.
---
---Available expanders:
---- `random`: Randomly selects a node group to scale.
---- `priority`: Selects the node group with the highest priority as per [user-provided configuration](https://docs.digitalocean.com/products/kubernetes/how-to/autoscale/#configuring-priority-expander)
---- `least_waste`: Selects the node group that will result in the least amount of idle resources.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfigurationExpandersList (digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfigurationExpandersItem|string)[]

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutput
---@field id string A unique ID that can be used to identify and reference a Kubernetes cluster.
---@field name string A human-readable name for a Kubernetes cluster.
---@field region string The slug identifier for the region where the Kubernetes cluster is located.
---@field version string The slug identifier for the version of Kubernetes used for the cluster. If set to a minor version (e.g. "1.14"), the latest version within it will be used (e.g. "1.14.6-do.1"); if set to "latest", the latest published version will be used. See the `/v2/kubernetes/options` endpoint to find all currently available versions.
---@field cluster_subnet string The range of IP addresses for the overlay network of the Kubernetes cluster in CIDR notation.
---@field service_subnet string The range of assignable IP addresses for services running in the Kubernetes cluster in CIDR notation.
---@field vpc_uuid string A string specifying the UUID of the VPC to which the Kubernetes cluster is assigned.<br><br>Requires `vpc:read` scope.
---@field worker_subnet_uuid? string The UUID of the VPC subnet to attach worker nodes to. When omitted on create, the default subnet for the VPC is used. This value cannot be changed after the cluster is created. `vpc_uuid` must also be set. <br><br>Requires `vpc:read` scope.
---@field ipv4 string The public IPv4 address of the Kubernetes master node. This will not be set if high availability is configured on the cluster (v1.21+)
---@field endpoint string The base URL of the API server on the Kubernetes master node.
---@field tags digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputTagsList An array of tags to apply to the Kubernetes cluster. All clusters are automatically tagged `k8s` and `k8s:$K8S_CLUSTER_ID`. <br><br>Requires `tag:read` and `tag:create` scope, as well as `tag:delete` if existing tags are getting removed.
---@field node_pools digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputNodePoolsList An object specifying the details of the worker nodes available to the Kubernetes cluster.
---@field maintenance_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.MaintenancePolicy|distilled.Null
---@field auto_upgrade? boolean A boolean value indicating whether the cluster will be automatically upgraded to new patch releases during its maintenance window.
---@field isolated_workers? boolean A boolean value indicating whether worker nodes in the cluster are not assigned public IP addresses. When omitted on create, the default value is false. When enabled, a NAT gateway must exist in the VPC where the cluster is created.
---@field gpu_operator_ready? boolean A boolean value indicating whether GPU nodes in the cluster are launched with images that do not include pre-installed GPU drivers, allowing GPU drivers to be managed by a GPU operator instead. Mutually exclusive with other GPU-related cluster options, such as `nvidia_gpu_dra_driver` and `amd_gpu_dra_driver`. When omitted on create, the default value is false.
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputStatus An object containing a `state` attribute whose value is set to a string indicating the current status of the cluster.
---@field created_at string A time value given in ISO8601 combined date and time format that represents when the Kubernetes cluster was created.
---@field updated_at? string A time value given in ISO8601 combined date and time format that represents when the Kubernetes cluster was last updated.
---@field surge_upgrade? boolean A boolean value indicating whether surge upgrade is enabled/disabled for the cluster. Surge upgrade makes cluster upgrades fast and reliable by bringing up new nodes before destroying the outdated nodes.
---@field ha? boolean A boolean value indicating whether the control plane is run in a highly available configuration in the cluster. Highly available control planes incur less downtime. The property cannot be disabled. When omitted on create, the default is version-dependent; for DOKS 1.36.0 and later, the default is true; for earlier versions, the default is false.
---@field registry_enabled? boolean A boolean value indicating whether GPU nodes in the cluster are launched with images that do not include pre-installed GPU drivers, allowing GPU drivers to be managed by a GPU operator instead. Mutually exclusive with other GPU-related cluster options, such as `nvidia_gpu_dra_driver` and `amd_gpu_dra_driver`. When omitted on create, the default value is false.
---@field control_plane_firewall? digitalocean.digitalocean.ControlPlaneFirewall|distilled.Null
---@field cluster_autoscaler_configuration? digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterAutoscalerConfiguration|distilled.Null
---@field sso? digitalocean.digitalocean.Sso|distilled.Null
---@field routing_agent? digitalocean.digitalocean.RoutingAgent|distilled.Null
---@field p2p_oci_registry_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.P2pOciRegistryPlugin|distilled.Null
---@field nfs_csi_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.NfsCsiPlugin|distilled.Null
---@field amd_gpu_device_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.AmdGpuDevicePlugin|distilled.Null
---@field amd_gpu_device_metrics_exporter_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.AmdGpuDeviceMetricsExporterPlugin|distilled.Null
---@field nvidia_gpu_device_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.NvidiaGpuDevicePlugin|distilled.Null
---@field nvidia_gpu_dra_driver? digitalocean.digitalocean.NvidiaGpuDraDriver|distilled.Null
---@field amd_gpu_dra_driver? digitalocean.digitalocean.AmdGpuDraDriver|distilled.Null
---@field rdma_shared_dev_plugin? digitalocean.digitalocean.RdmaSharedDevPlugin|distilled.Null
---@field coredns_autoscaler? digitalocean.digitalocean.CorednsAutoscaler|distilled.Null

---An object specifying the details of the worker nodes available to the Kubernetes cluster.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputNodePoolsList digitalocean.digitalocean.KubernetesNodePool[]

---An object containing a `state` attribute whose value is set to a string indicating the current status of the cluster.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputStatus
---@field state? digitalocean.digitalocean.ClusterOutputStatusState A string indicating the current status of the cluster.
---@field message? string An optional message providing additional information about the current cluster state.

