---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionRequest
---@field openai_session_id? string OpenAI Agents API session id (sess_…) for adapter: codex-agentapi. doctl creates the OpenAI session before calling DO and passes the resulting id here; harness-api persists it for correlation. Empty/omitted for every other agent kind.
---@field resume_on_topoff? boolean Opt the new session in to automatic resumption when the team's prepayment balance is restored. Defaults to false. Exists as a query parameter so the environment spec (YAML body) form can carry it too. On the application/json form the body field is idiomatic, but this parameter wins when both are present. Must be exactly one of true/false/1/0; anything else is a 400.
---@field xDeviceUUID? string Optional hardware device id forwarded by doctl. Persisted on the session row for lifecycle attribution. Values over 128 bytes are ignored.
---@field name string Session name, independent of the config name. Must satisfy the existing environment-spec metadata.name rules and must not be UUID-shaped.
---@field config_id string
---@field region? string Optional placement check, not a placement choice: the session is always created in the region whose API host served the request. If set, it must equal that region, or the request fails with 400 and a region_mismatch message. Honored only for teams on the regional routing rollout; ignored otherwise.
---@field workspace_id? string Optional persistent workspace to attach at create; its files are mounted at `/workspace`. The workspace must be `AVAILABLE`, otherwise the request returns 409. Accepted only in this JSON form; an environment spec that contains workspace_id is rejected with 400. Returns 403 when persistent workspaces are not enabled for the team.

