---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequest
---@field serverRef string Identifier for the server, unique within your team. Must match `^`[a-z]``[a-z0-9-]`{0,63}$`.
---@field endpoint string HTTPS URL of the server's MCP endpoint. Its host must resolve only to public IP addresses. Required.
---@field transport? digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestTransport|string Optional. `streamable_http`, the default and only accepted value.
---@field credentialRefSource? digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestCredentialRefSource|string How requests to the server authenticate: none (the default), secret, or connection. With secret, the value from `credentialRef` or `api_key` is sent in the Authorization header, prefixed with "Bearer " unless it already contains a space.
---@field description? string Optional description shown on the server's catalog card. At most 1024 characters.
---@field credentialRef? string For `credentialRefSource` secret: a reference to a secret your team stores with DigitalOcean. Must match `^`[A-Za-z0-9]``[A-Za-z0-9:/_.-]`{0,254}$`. Set exactly one of `credentialRef` and `api_key`.
---@field api_key? string|distilled.Secret For `credentialRefSource` secret: the key or token itself. DigitalOcean stores it; it is write-only and no response returns it. Set exactly one of `credentialRef` and `api_key`.
---@field oauth_client_id? string Required for `credentialRefSource` connection: the client ID of your team's OAuth client for the server. Each user of the server then authorizes individually.
---@field oauth_client_secret? string|distilled.Secret Required for `credentialRefSource` connection. Write-only; no response returns it.
---@field oauth_authorize_url? string Required for `credentialRefSource` connection: the OAuth authorization endpoint. It must use the endpoint's scheme and port, on the endpoint's host or another host under the same registrable domain.
---@field oauth_token_url? string Required for `credentialRefSource` connection: the OAuth token endpoint, under the same rules as `oauth_authorize_url`.
---@field oauth_scopes? digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestOauthScopesList Required for `credentialRefSource` connection: the scopes to request from each user, 1 to 64 of them.
---@field oauth_authorization_ttl_seconds? string How long, in seconds, a user's authorization may be reused before they must consent again. Optional; 0 means 30 days, and the maximum is 100 years. Authorizations are not refreshed automatically, so this window, not the provider's token lifetime, decides how often a user is sent back through consent. Set it no longer than the provider's own token lifetime, so the prompt arrives before a tool call fails against an expired token.

---How requests to the server authenticate: none (the default), secret, or connection. With secret, the value from `credentialRef` or `api_key` is sent in the Authorization header, prefixed with "Bearer " unless it already contains a space.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestCredentialRefSource "none"|"secret"|"connection"

---Required for `credentialRefSource` connection: the scopes to request from each user, 1 to 64 of them.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestOauthScopesList string[]

---Optional. `streamable_http`, the default and only accepted value.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequestTransport "streamable_http"

