---An Insights dashboard.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Dashboard
---@field uuid string A unique identifier for the dashboard.
---@field name? string The dashboard's display name. Populated by the server from `spec.display.name`; it cannot be set directly. Omitted when `spec.display.name` is an empty string.
---@field description? string The dashboard's display description. Populated by the server from `spec.display.description`; it cannot be set directly. Omitted when the spec has no description.
---@field spec string The dashboard definition as a JSON document serialized to a string. The document must have `kind` set to `Dashboard` and a `spec.display.name` between 1 and 255 characters, which is projected to `name`. An optional `spec.display.description` of up to 1000 characters is projected to `description`. Retrieve the full JSON Schema from `GET /v2/insights/dashboards/schema`. The document is returned in a normalized form: content is unchanged, but object keys may be reordered and whitespace may differ from the submitted string.
---@field created_at string Time the dashboard was created.
---@field updated_at string Time the dashboard was last updated.

---Error body returned by the dashboards service. Unlike most DigitalOcean API errors, this body carries a gRPC status code rather than an `id` string.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.DashboardError
---@field error string A human-readable description of the error. Identical to `message`.
---@field message string A human-readable description of the error. Identical to `error`.
---@field code number The gRPC status code for the error. `3` = invalid argument, `5` = not found, `6` = already exists, `8` = resource exhausted, `13` = internal.
---@field details? digitalocean.digitalocean.DashboardErrorDetailsList Additional machine-readable error details. Omitted when there are none. Each entry carries an `@type` identifying its schema.

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.DashboardErrorDetailsItemMap { [string]: any }

