---Session is the user-facing record of a environment session + sandbox pair.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsSession
---@field session_id string
---@field name? string User-assignable display name, unique per team among non-terminal sessions. Usable in place of session_id by clients (doctl / Console resolve it to the id via the ListSessions ?name= filter; the {session_id} path stays UUID-only). Supplied via the environment-spec metadata.name, or auto-generated ("session-<agent-type>-<date-time>") when omitted.
---@field parent_session_id? string Lineage: id of the session this one was forked from. Omitted/empty for root (non-fork) sessions.
---@field fork_id? string Lineage: branch label assigned when this session was created by ForkSession (or rollback's internal fork). Omitted/empty for root sessions.
---@field fork_from_checkpoint_id? string Lineage: harness-api checkpoint id (cp_<hex>) the child booted from at fork time. Drives OHP inherited-history replay on attach. Omitted/empty for root sessions and legacy forks created before this field was persisted.
---@field agent_kind? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentKind
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.SessionStatus
---@field sandbox_id? string Sandbox identity for support / debugging. Informational; omitted until a sandbox is allocated.
---@field created_at? string
---@field last_event_at? string Timestamp of the most recent event in this session's canonical stream. Drives the inactivity policy that pauses idle sessions.
---@field keep_warm? boolean Session is exempt from idle auto-pause (manifest keep_warm, or the agent-kind default: hermes sessions keep warm). It still accepts a manual pause. Omitted when false.
---@field resume_on_topoff? boolean Session consents to being resumed automatically when the team's prepayment balance is restored after a low-balance pause. Defaults to false at create time; may be toggled later via PATCH /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id} (resume_on_topoff only). Only a session paused with reason low_balance whose latest run did not complete is ever resumed automatically - a session the customer paused themselves, or one that idled out, stays paused regardless. Not an environment-spec field, and forks do not inherit it. Omitted when false.
---@field pause_reason? string Why this session is paused. Present only when status is SESSION_STATUS_PAUSED; omitted otherwise. Known values: manual (PauseSession RPC), idle (inactivity auto-pause), low_balance (prepay gate). Clients should treat an unrecognized value as an opaque reason string.
---@field idle_timeout_seconds? number This session's own idle-pause timeout (manifest idle_timeout). Omitted when the session uses the deployment-wide default.
---@field repo_hint? string Optional repository hint supplied at session creation (first spec.workspace.repos entry of the manifest). Not authoritative; the agent may change repos in-session.
---@field warnings? digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsSessionWarningsList Non-fatal advisories computed from the manifest at create time: one entry per populated accepted-but-not-yet-enforced section (flat names: secrets, model, tools, memory, budget, max_lifetime, mounts; legacy manifests get the corresponding spec.* paths), a deprecation entry when a legacy-envelope manifest or an adapter alias (codex-cli, cursor-cli) is used, and a heuristic entry per credential-looking spec.env value. Populated on the CreateSession response only.
---@field config_id? string Durable Environment Config UUID the session was created from (inline manifests persist a config too, named after the session). Persisted and returned on create/get/list; absent only for sessions created before config references were stored.
---@field openai_session_id? string OpenAI Agents API session id (sess_…) this DO sandbox hosts. Populated only for AGENT_KIND_OPENAI_CODEX sessions (empty otherwise). Non-secret correlation metadata; a client (doctl agents attach) reads it to bridge to the OpenAI session. See docs/design/openai-sandbox-provider.md.
---@field openai_environment_id? string OpenAI Agents API environment id (env_…), captured from the resolved CODEX_ENVIRONMENT_ID guest env value. Populated only for AGENT_KIND_OPENAI_CODEX sessions. Non-secret correlation metadata.
---@field region? string DO region slug the session lives in, e.g. ric1. Stamped once at create from the region whose API host served the request, and never changed. Returned only for teams on the regional routing rollout; omitted otherwise.
---@field workspace_id? string The persistent workspace attached to the session, mounted at `/workspace`. Empty when the session has none. Fork and rollback return 409 for a session that has a workspace.
---@field update? digitalocean.digitalocean.SessionConfigUpdate
---@field config_drifted? boolean True when the running config differs from the manifest the session was created from, for example after a successful PATCH with `manifest_yaml`. Omitted when false.
---@field config_diff? digitalocean.digitalocean.SessionConfigChanges
---@field manifest? digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsSessionManifestMap The effective manifest of the session. Present only when `config_drifted` is true. Never contains secret values.

---The effective manifest of the session. Present only when `config_drifted` is true. Never contains secret values.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsSessionManifestMap { [string]: any }

---Non-fatal advisories computed from the manifest at create time: one entry per populated accepted-but-not-yet-enforced section (flat names: secrets, model, tools, memory, budget, max_lifetime, mounts; legacy manifests get the corresponding spec.* paths), a deprecation entry when a legacy-envelope manifest or an adapter alias (codex-cli, cursor-cli) is used, and a heuristic entry per credential-looking spec.env value. Populated on the CreateSession response only.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsSessionWarningsList string[]

