---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletImage
---@field id? number A unique number that can be used to identify and reference a specific image.
---@field name? string
---@field type? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletImageType Describes the kind of image. It may be one of `base`, `snapshot`, `backup`, `custom`, or `admin`. Respectively, this specifies whether an image is a DigitalOcean base OS image, user-generated Droplet snapshot, automatically created Droplet backup, user-provided virtual machine image, or an image used for DigitalOcean managed resources (e.g. DOKS worker nodes).
---@field distribution? digitalocean.digitalocean.Distribution
---@field slug? string|distilled.Null A uniquely identifying string that is associated with each of the DigitalOcean-provided public images. These can be used to reference a public image as an alternative to the numeric id.
---@field public? boolean This is a boolean value that indicates whether the image in question is public or not. An image that is public is available to all accounts. A non-public image is only accessible from your account.
---@field regions? digitalocean.digitalocean.RegionsArray
---@field created_at? string A time value given in ISO8601 combined date and time format that represents when the image was created.
---@field min_disk_size? number|distilled.Null The minimum disk size in GB required for a Droplet to use this image.
---@field size_gigabytes? number|distilled.Null The size of the image in gigabytes.
---@field description? string
---@field tags? digitalocean.digitalocean.TagsArray|distilled.Null
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletImageStatus A status string indicating the state of a custom image. This may be `NEW`, `available`, `pending`, `deleted`, or `retired`.
---@field error_message? string A string containing information about errors that may occur when importing a custom image.

---A status string indicating the state of a custom image. This may be `NEW`,
--- `available`, `pending`, `deleted`, or `retired`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletImageStatus "NEW"|"available"|"pending"|"deleted"|"retired"

---Describes the kind of image. It may be one of `base`, `snapshot`, `backup`, `custom`, or `admin`. Respectively, this specifies whether an image is a DigitalOcean base OS image, user-generated Droplet snapshot, automatically created Droplet backup, user-provided virtual machine image, or an image used for DigitalOcean managed resources (e.g. DOKS worker nodes).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletImageType "base"|"snapshot"|"backup"|"custom"|"admin"

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInput
---@field names digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputNamesList An array of human human-readable strings you wish to use when displaying the Droplet name. Each name, if set to a domain name managed in the DigitalOcean DNS management system, will configure a PTR record for the Droplet. Each name set during creation will also determine the hostname for the Droplet in its internal configuration.
---@field region? string The slug identifier for the region that you wish to deploy the Droplet in. If the specific datacenter is not not important, a slug prefix (e.g. `nyc`) can be used to deploy the Droplet in any of the that region's locations (`nyc1`, `nyc2`, or `nyc3`). If the region is omitted from the create request completely, the Droplet may deploy in any region.
---@field size string The slug identifier for the size that you wish to select for this Droplet.
---@field image digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputImage The image ID of a public or private image or the slug identifier for a public image. This image will be the base image for your Droplet.<br>Requires `image:read` scope.
---@field ssh_keys? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputSshKeysList An array containing the IDs or fingerprints of the SSH keys that you wish to embed in the Droplet's root account upon creation. You must add the keys to your team before they can be embedded on a Droplet.<br>Requires `ssh_key:read` scope.
---@field backups? boolean A boolean indicating whether automated backups should be enabled for the Droplet.
---@field backup_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputBackupPolicy
---@field ipv6? boolean A boolean indicating whether to enable IPv6 on the Droplet.
---@field monitoring? boolean A boolean indicating whether to install the DigitalOcean agent for monitoring.
---@field tags? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputTagsList|distilled.Null A flat array of tag names as strings to apply to the Droplet after it is created. Tag names can either be existing or new tags.<br>Requires `tag:create` scope.
---@field user_data? string A string containing 'user data' which may be used to configure the Droplet on first boot, often a 'cloud-config' file or Bash script. It must be plain text and may not exceed 64 KiB in size.
---@field private_networking? boolean This parameter has been deprecated. Use `vpc_uuid` instead to specify a VPC network for the Droplet. If no `vpc_uuid` is provided, the Droplet will be placed in your account's default VPC for the region.
---@field volumes? digitalocean.digitalocean.DropletMultiCreateInputVolumesList An array of IDs for block storage volumes that will be attached to the Droplet once created. The volumes must not already be attached to an existing Droplet.<br>Requires `block_storage:read` scpoe.
---@field vpc_uuid? string A string specifying the UUID of the VPC to which the Droplet will be assigned. If excluded, the Droplet will be assigned to your account's default VPC for the region.<br>Requires `vpc:read` scope.
---@field subnet_uuid? string An optional string specifying the UUID of the VPC subnet to which the Droplet will be assigned. If excluded, the Droplet will be assigned to a default subnet of the VPC.<br>Requires `vpc:read` scope.
---@field with_droplet_agent? boolean A boolean indicating whether to install the DigitalOcean agent used for providing access to the Droplet web console in the control panel. By default, the agent is installed on new Droplets but installation errors (i.e. OS not supported) are ignored. To prevent it from being installed, set to `false`. To make installation errors fatal, explicitly set it to `true`.
---@field public_networking? boolean An optional boolean indicating whether this Droplet should be created with public networking or not. By default, all Droplets are created with public networking available. If explicitly set to `false`, only private networking will be enabled, and public networking will be disabled; currently this means that it will not have any public static or Reserved IPv4 or IPv6 address, nor can one be assigned later. If explicitly set to `false`, `ipv6` must also be `false`.

