---A named lineage of immutable versions owned by its creating user. Only that user may use it, update it, create versions, or promote versions. A team owner may also list and delete team endpoints, but may not use them or add versions. Service-managed endpoints and their versions are not part of the public API: lists and search omit them, every read or write of one returns the same 404 as an unknown ID, and deleting one returns the same 204 as deleting an unknown ID without changing it. Deletion is final for this identity and all cascaded version identities; retries, replays, and later writes cannot resurrect them. Reusing identical contents after endpoint deletion requires a new endpoint identity and a new version identity and number.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Endpoint
---@field id string
---@field name string
---@field actor_id string Immutable actor binding; empty means no actor.
---@field is_default? boolean True only for your own default endpoint in the team: the one the generic MCP URL and data-plane requests without `X-Session-Id` or `X-Endpoint-Id` resolve to for you, which Action Gateway creates on first use. False for every other endpoint, including other team members' default endpoints that a team owner can see, so a response marks at most one endpoint. A default endpoint does not count toward your team's endpoint limit or reserve its name. After it is deleted, the next such request creates a new default. Returned in responses only.
---@field head_version? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersion|distilled.Null Embedded live head version, the highest-numbered live version. Null when no live version remains.
---@field insights? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointInsights|distilled.Null
---@field mcp_url? string MCP URL that resolves the highest-numbered live version on every request. Its host follows the head version's VPC region, or the default host when no version is live. It is the same value the create response returns as mcp_url. Returned in responses only.
---@field created_at string When the endpoint was created.
---@field updated_at string When the endpoint was last changed.

---Version options, stored and returned as supplied. Omission leaves config absent; an explicit empty object is preserved. Property names are camelCase, as in the session API; other keys are stored but have no effect.
