---An immutable, live endpoint version. Its ID must encode endpoint_id and version_number. Deleting it does not reuse its number or change older versions. Deletion is final: retries, replays, and later writes cannot resurrect its identity. Identical contents require a new version identity and number. Omitted tools means every tool; a present selection with empty references means no tools. Policy and config retain omission versus explicitly empty objects.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersion
---@field id string
---@field endpoint_id string
---@field version_number number
---@field promoted_from_version_number? number
---@field name string The endpoint's name when this version was created. Renaming the endpoint does not change it.
---@field actor_id string Actor binding shared by every version of the endpoint; empty means no actor.
---@field policy digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointPolicy|distilled.Null
---@field tools? digitalocean.digitalocean.Tools Canonical pinned selection; omitted means every tool, empty references means none.
---@field config? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointConfig
---@field network? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointNetworkResponse
---@field insights? digitalocean.digitalocean.SessionInsights Deprecated: always omitted. Versions do not carry Insights consent; read the endpoint's insights instead.
---@field mcp_url? string Pinned MCP URL for this version, valid for the version's lifetime. It is the same value the create response returns as version_mcp_url. Its final segment is the backing session UUID, not the composite version ID. VPC-bound versions may use a regional host. Returned in responses only.
---@field created_at string When the version was created.
---@field updated_at string When the version was last updated.

---Returns one immutable live version.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersionResponse
---@field version digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersion

---Immutable version configuration. The endpoint owner and actor cannot change between versions. Omitted or empty actor_id means no actor binding.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersionSpec
---@field actor_id? string Actor whose provider connections are used. Omitted or empty means no actor.
---@field policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointPolicy|distilled.Null
---@field tools? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointVersionSpecToolsList Omitted enables every tool; an explicit empty array enables no tools. Direct tools use provider-qualified slugs, optionally pinned as tool@version. Toolbelts must be pinned as toolbelt:name@version. Floating pins are rejected.
---@field config? digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointConfig
