---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetHarnessSessionEventsRequest
---@field session_id string The session UUID.
---@field replay_only? boolean Write the selected history and then close the stream, rather than going live. Does not advance the device's delivery cursor, so it never supersedes a live attach from the same device.
---@field replay_from? string Event-id pagination cursor for the `replay_only` lane only; return events after this one. There is no last-N floor, so a cursor already at the head yields nothing. Ignored on a live attach.
---@field cursor? string Query-param equivalent of `Last-Event-ID`, because a browser EventSource cannot set request headers. Takes precedence over the header when both are present. Live-attach lane only.
---@field device_id? string Query-param equivalent of `X-Device-UUID`. Identifies one client install so its delivery cursor and live slot are its own; a second attach from the same device supersedes the first.
---@field lastEventID? string The last event this client rendered (not merely received). Its presence marks the request a reconnect, so OHP serves strictly what follows it with no last-N floor. Persist it only after rendering.
---@field xDeviceUUID? string A stable per-install device id. See `device_id`.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetHarnessSessionEventsResponse

