---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthRequest
---@field tool_slug string Catalog tool slug, for example `exa_search`. Required.
---@field window? digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthRequestWindow|string Window to aggregate over. Defaults to twenty-four hours. - `HEALTH_WINDOW_UNSPECIFIED`: Twenty-four hours. - `HEALTH_WINDOW_ONE_HOUR`: One hour; history points are 10 minutes. - `HEALTH_WINDOW_TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS`: Twenty-four hours; history points are 1 hour. - `HEALTH_WINDOW_SEVEN_DAYS`: Seven days; history points are 6 hours. - `HEALTH_WINDOW_THIRTY_DAYS`: Thirty days; history points are 24 hours.
---@field include_history? boolean Additionally returns the window split into resolution-aligned points (the history field below).

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthRequestWindow "HEALTH_WINDOW_ONE_HOUR"|"HEALTH_WINDOW_TWENTY_FOUR_HOURS"|"HEALTH_WINDOW_SEVEN_DAYS"|"HEALTH_WINDOW_THIRTY_DAYS"

---Health of one tool.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponse
---@field snapshot? digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthSnapshot When the metrics were computed and the window they cover.
---@field tool? digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolHealth The tool's metrics over the window.
---@field history? digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistory|distilled.Null Present only when the request set `include_history`.

---Present only when the request set `include_history`.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistory
---@field resolution? string Length of each point.
---@field stale? boolean Means the same as HealthSnapshot.stale, for the history series. The series is refreshed independently, so a fresh snapshot can accompany an older history and vice versa.
---@field points? digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistoryPointsList Points oldest first, ending with the slot in progress.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistoryPointsItem
---@field bucket_start? string Start of the slot.
---@field health? digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthMetrics Metrics over the slot.

---Points oldest first, ending with the slot in progress.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistoryPointsList digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolHealthResponseHistoryPointsItem[]

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolbeltRequest
---@field name string Toolbelt name.
---@field version? string Version number to read. Empty returns the latest version.
---@field page_size? number Page size for `tool_details` only; toolbelt.tools always lists every member. Defaults to 20; values above 100 are capped at 100.
---@field page_token? string `next_page_token` from the previous response, to continue `tool_details`. Treat it as opaque, and send it only with the same toolbelt, version, and search.
---@field search? string Restricts `tool_details` to members whose tool slug, name, title, description, provider, or category contains this value, case-insensitively. It does not filter toolbelt.tools. This is a substring match, not a filter expression.

---Returns one toolbelt version and a page of member details.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolbeltResponse
---@field toolbelt digitalocean.digitalocean.Toolbelt
---@field tool_details? digitalocean.digitalocean.GetToolbeltResponseToolDetailsList The requested page of resolved catalog metadata for the members named in toolbelt.tools. It is a page, so it is not the membership of the toolbelt: read toolbelt.tools for that, and toolbelt.tool_count for the total. Ordering matches toolbelt.tools.
