---An object specifying health check settings for the load balancer.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthCheck
---@field protocol? digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthCheckProtocol|string The protocol used for health checks sent to the backend Droplets. The possible values are `http`, `https`, or `tcp`.
---@field port? number An integer representing the port on the backend Droplets on which the health check will attempt a connection.
---@field path? string The path on the backend Droplets to which the load balancer instance will send a request.
---@field check_interval_seconds? number The number of seconds between between two consecutive health checks.
---@field response_timeout_seconds? number The number of seconds the load balancer instance will wait for a response until marking a health check as failed.
---@field unhealthy_threshold? number The number of times a health check must fail for a backend Droplet to be marked "unhealthy" and be removed from the pool.
---@field healthy_threshold? number The number of times a health check must pass for a backend Droplet to be marked "healthy" and be re-added to the pool.

---The protocol used for health checks sent to the backend Droplets. The possible values are `http`, `https`, or `tcp`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthCheckProtocol "http"|"https"|"tcp"

---Availability and latency of a tool or provider over a window, aggregated across all customers. Request volumes are not reported.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthMetrics
---@field data_status? digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthMetricsDataStatus `HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_AVAILABLE` when the window has calls to measure; `HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_NO_DATA` when it has none, in which case the metrics are null. Do not treat no data as healthy.
---@field uptime_percentage? number|distilled.Null Percentage of calls that did not fail because of the provider (an upstream error, timeout, rate limit, or unavailability). Calls that failed for other reasons are not counted.
---@field latency_p50_ms? number|distilled.Null Median duration of successful calls, in milliseconds. Durations above 40960 ms are reported as 40960.
---@field latency_p95_ms? number|distilled.Null 95th-percentile duration of successful calls, in milliseconds. Durations above 40960 ms are reported as 40960.

---`HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_AVAILABLE` when the window has calls to measure; `HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_NO_DATA` when it has none, in which case the metrics are null. Do not treat no data as healthy.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthMetricsDataStatus "HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_AVAILABLE"|"HEALTH_DATA_STATUS_NO_DATA"

---Describes when health metrics were computed.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthSnapshot
---@field measured_at? string|distilled.Null When the metrics were computed. They are recomputed at most every five minutes.
---@field window? string Length of the window the metrics cover, ending at `measured_at`.
---@field stale? boolean True when the latest recomputation failed and earlier metrics, up to 30 minutes old, are returned instead.

