---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfig
---@field compression_type? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigCompressionType|string Specify the final compression type for a given topic. This configuration accepts the standard compression codecs ('gzip', 'snappy', 'lz4', 'zstd'). It additionally accepts 'uncompressed' which is equivalent to no compression; and 'producer' which means retain the original compression codec set by the producer.
---@field group_initial_rebalance_delay_ms? number The amount of time, in milliseconds, the group coordinator will wait for more consumers to join a new group before performing the first rebalance. A longer delay means potentially fewer rebalances, but increases the time until processing begins. The default value for this is 3 seconds. During development and testing it might be desirable to set this to 0 in order to not delay test execution time.
---@field group_min_session_timeout_ms? number The minimum allowed session timeout for registered consumers. Longer timeouts give consumers more time to process messages in between heartbeats at the cost of a longer time to detect failures.
---@field group_max_session_timeout_ms? number The maximum allowed session timeout for registered consumers. Longer timeouts give consumers more time to process messages in between heartbeats at the cost of a longer time to detect failures.
---@field connections_max_idle_ms? number Idle connections timeout: the server socket processor threads close the connections that idle for longer than this.
---@field max_incremental_fetch_session_cache_slots? number The maximum number of incremental fetch sessions that the broker will maintain.
---@field message_max_bytes? number The maximum size of message that the server can receive.
---@field offsets_retention_minutes? number Log retention window in minutes for offsets topic
---@field log_cleaner_delete_retention_ms? number How long are delete records retained?
---@field log_cleaner_min_cleanable_ratio? number Controls log compactor frequency. Larger value means more frequent compactions but also more space wasted for logs. Consider setting log_cleaner_max_compaction_lag_ms to enforce compactions sooner, instead of setting a very high value for this option.
---@field log_cleaner_max_compaction_lag_ms? number The maximum amount of time message will remain uncompacted. Only applicable for logs that are being compacted
---@field log_cleaner_min_compaction_lag_ms? number The minimum time a message will remain uncompacted in the log. Only applicable for logs that are being compacted.
---@field log_cleanup_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigLogCleanupPolicy|string The default cleanup policy for segments beyond the retention window
---@field log_flush_interval_messages? number The number of messages accumulated on a log partition before messages are flushed to disk
---@field log_flush_interval_ms? number The maximum time in ms that a message in any topic is kept in memory before flushed to disk. If not set, the value in log.flush.scheduler.interval.ms is used
---@field log_index_interval_bytes? number The interval with which Kafka adds an entry to the offset index
---@field log_index_size_max_bytes? number The maximum size in bytes of the offset index
---@field log_message_downconversion_enable? boolean This configuration controls whether down-conversion of message formats is enabled to satisfy consume requests.
---@field log_message_timestamp_type? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigLogMessageTimestampType|string Define whether the timestamp in the message is message create time or log append time.
---@field log_message_timestamp_difference_max_ms? number The maximum difference allowed between the timestamp when a broker receives a message and the timestamp specified in the message
---@field log_preallocate? boolean Controls whether to preallocate a file when creating a new segment
---@field log_retention_bytes? number The maximum size of the log before deleting messages
---@field log_retention_hours? number The number of hours to keep a log file before deleting it
---@field log_retention_ms? number The number of milliseconds to keep a log file before deleting it (in milliseconds), If not set, the value in log.retention.minutes is used. If set to -1, no time limit is applied.
---@field log_roll_jitter_ms? number The maximum jitter to subtract from logRollTimeMillis (in milliseconds). If not set, the value in log.roll.jitter.hours is used
---@field log_roll_ms? number The maximum time before a new log segment is rolled out (in milliseconds).
---@field log_segment_bytes? number The maximum size of a single log file
---@field log_segment_delete_delay_ms? number The amount of time to wait before deleting a file from the filesystem
---@field auto_create_topics_enable? boolean Enable auto creation of topics
---@field min_insync_replicas? number When a producer sets acks to 'all' (or '-1'), min_insync_replicas specifies the minimum number of replicas that must acknowledge a write for the write to be considered successful.
---@field num_partitions? number Number of partitions for autocreated topics
---@field default_replication_factor? number Replication factor for autocreated topics
---@field replica_fetch_max_bytes? number The number of bytes of messages to attempt to fetch for each partition (defaults to 1048576). This is not an absolute maximum, if the first record batch in the first non-empty partition of the fetch is larger than this value, the record batch will still be returned to ensure that progress can be made.
---@field replica_fetch_response_max_bytes? number Maximum bytes expected for the entire fetch response (defaults to 10485760). Records are fetched in batches, and if the first record batch in the first non-empty partition of the fetch is larger than this value, the record batch will still be returned to ensure that progress can be made. As such, this is not an absolute maximum.
---@field max_connections_per_ip? number The maximum number of connections allowed from each ip address (defaults to 2147483647).
---@field producer_purgatory_purge_interval_requests? number The purge interval (in number of requests) of the producer request purgatory (defaults to 1000).
---@field socket_request_max_bytes? number The maximum number of bytes in a socket request (defaults to 104857600).
---@field transaction_state_log_segment_bytes? number The transaction topic segment bytes should be kept relatively small in order to facilitate faster log compaction and cache loads (defaults to 104857600 (100 mebibytes)).
---@field transaction_remove_expired_transaction_cleanup_interval_ms? number The interval at which to remove transactions that have expired due to transactional.id.expiration.ms passing (defaults to 3600000 (1 hour)).
---@field schema_registry? boolean Enable creation of schema registry for the Kafka cluster. Schema_registry only works with General Purpose - Dedicated CPU plans.

---Specify the final compression type for a given topic. This configuration accepts the standard compression codecs ('gzip', 'snappy', 'lz4', 'zstd'). It additionally accepts 'uncompressed' which is equivalent to no compression; and 'producer' which means retain the original compression codec set by the producer.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigCompressionType "gzip"|"snappy"|"lz4"|"zstd"|"uncompressed"|"producer"

---The default cleanup policy for segments beyond the retention window
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigLogCleanupPolicy "delete"|"compact"|"compact,delete"

---Define whether the timestamp in the message is message create time or log append time.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaAdvancedConfigLogMessageTimestampType "CreateTime"|"LogAppendTime"

