---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopic
---@field name? string The name of the Kafka topic.
---@field replication_factor? number The number of nodes to replicate data across the cluster.
---@field partition_count? number The number of partitions available for the topic. On update, this value can only be increased.
---@field state? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicState The state of the Kafka topic.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfig
---@field cleanup_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigCleanupPolicy|string The cleanup_policy sets the retention policy to use on log segments. 'delete' will discard old segments when retention time/size limits are reached. 'compact' will enable log compaction, resulting in retention of the latest value for each key.
---@field compression_type? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigCompressionType|string The compression_type specifies the compression type of the topic.
---@field delete_retention_ms? number The delete_retention_ms specifies how long (in ms) to retain delete tombstone markers for topics.
---@field file_delete_delay_ms? number The file_delete_delay_ms specifies the time (in ms) to wait before deleting a file from the filesystem.
---@field flush_messages? number The flush_messages specifies the number of messages to accumulate on a log partition before messages are flushed to disk.
---@field flush_ms? number The flush_ms specifies the maximum time (in ms) that a message is kept in memory before being flushed to disk.
---@field index_interval_bytes? number The index_interval_bytes specifies the number of bytes between entries being added into te offset index.
---@field max_compaction_lag_ms? number The max_compaction_lag_ms specifies the maximum amount of time (in ms) that a message will remain uncompacted. This is only applicable if the logs are have compaction enabled.
---@field max_message_bytes? number The max_messages_bytes specifies the largest record batch size (in bytes) that can be sent to the server. This is calculated after compression if compression is enabled.
---@field message_down_conversion_enable? boolean The message_down_conversion_enable specifies whether down-conversion of message formats is enabled to satisfy consumer requests. When 'false', the broker will not perform conversion for consumers expecting older message formats. The broker will respond with an `UNSUPPORTED_VERSION` error for consume requests from these older clients.
---@field message_format_version? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigMessageFormatVersion|string The message_format_version specifies the message format version used by the broker to append messages to the logs. The value of this setting is assumed to be 3.0-IV1 if the broker protocol version is 3.0 or higher. By setting a particular message format version, all existing messages on disk must be smaller or equal to the specified version.
---@field message_timestamp_type? digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigMessageTimestampType|string The message_timestamp_type specifies whether to use the message create time or log append time as the timestamp on a message.
---@field min_cleanable_dirty_ratio? number The min_cleanable_dirty_ratio specifies the frequency of log compaction (if enabled) in relation to duplicates present in the logs. For example, at 0.5, at most 50% of the log could be duplicates before compaction would begin.
---@field min_compaction_lag_ms? number The min_compaction_lag_ms specifies the minimum time (in ms) that a message will remain uncompacted in the log. Only relevant if log compaction is enabled.
---@field min_insync_replicas? number The min_insync_replicas specifies the number of replicas that must ACK a write for the write to be considered successful.
---@field preallocate? boolean The preallocate specifies whether a file should be preallocated on disk when creating a new log segment.
---@field retention_bytes? number The retention_bytes specifies the maximum size of the log (in bytes) before deleting messages. -1 indicates that there is no limit.
---@field retention_ms? number The retention_ms specifies the maximum amount of time (in ms) to keep a message before deleting it.
---@field segment_bytes? number The segment_bytes specifies the maximum size of a single log file (in bytes).
---@field segment_jitter_ms? number The segment_jitter_ms specifies the maximum random jitter subtracted from the scheduled segment roll time to avoid thundering herds of segment rolling.
---@field segment_ms? number The segment_ms specifies the period of time after which the log will be forced to roll if the segment file isn't full. This ensures that retention can delete or compact old data.

---The cleanup_policy sets the retention policy to use on log segments. 'delete' will discard old segments when retention time/size limits are reached. 'compact' will enable log compaction, resulting in retention of the latest value for each key.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigCleanupPolicy "delete"|"compact"|"compact_delete"

---The compression_type specifies the compression type of the topic.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigCompressionType "producer"|"gzip"|"snappy"|"Iz4"|"zstd"|"uncompressed"

---The message_format_version specifies the message format version used by the broker to append messages to the logs. The value of this setting is assumed to be 3.0-IV1 if the broker protocol version is 3.0 or higher. By setting a  particular message format version, all existing messages on disk must be smaller or equal to the specified version.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigMessageFormatVersion "0.8.0"|"0.8.1"|"0.8.2"|"0.9.0"|"0.10.0-IV0"|"0.10.0-IV1"|"0.10.1-IV0"|"0.10.1-IV1"|"0.10.1-IV2"|"0.10.2-IV0"|"0.11.0-IV0"|"0.11.0-IV1"|"0.11.0-IV2"|"1.0-IV0"|"1.1-IV0"|"2.0-IV0"|"2.0-IV1"|"2.1-IV0"|"2.1-IV1"|"2.1-IV2"|"2.2-IV0"|"2.2-IV1"|"2.3-IV0"|"2.3-IV1"|"2.4-IV0"|"2.4-IV1"|"2.5-IV0"|"2.6-IV0"|"2.7-IV0"|"2.7-IV1"|"2.7-IV2"|"2.8-IV0"|"2.8-IV1"|"3.0-IV0"|"3.0-IV1"|"3.1-IV0"|"3.2-IV0"|"3.3-IV0"|"3.3-IV1"|"3.3-IV2"|"3.3-IV3"

---The message_timestamp_type specifies whether to use the message create time or log append time as the timestamp on a message.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.KafkaTopicConfigMessageTimestampType "create_time"|"log_append_time"

