---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2Request
---@field page? number Page number for pagination.
---@field per_page? number Number of items per page.
---@field search? string Optional partial, case-insensitive match on the display name or model ID. Omit this when filtering only by modality, serving, or product.
---@field serving? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestServingList Filter by where the model is served. Multiple values use OR semantics. - MODEL_SERVING_SERVERLESS: Serverless inference. - MODEL_SERVING_DEDICATED: Dedicated inference.
---@field badges? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestBadgesList Filter by badge. Multiple values use OR semantics. - MODEL_CATALOG_BADGE_FEATURED: Featured in the catalog. - MODEL_CATALOG_BADGE_NEW: Newly added. - MODEL_CATALOG_BADGE_PREVIEW: Preview. - MODEL_CATALOG_BADGE_DEPRECATING: Scheduled for deprecation. - MODEL_CATALOG_BADGE_INFERENCE_ROUTER: Inference Router preset.
---@field input_modality? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestInputModalityList Require every listed modality as a model input. Multiple values use AND semantics. - MODEL_MODALITY_TEXT: plain text - MODEL_MODALITY_IMAGE: still images - MODEL_MODALITY_AUDIO: audio - MODEL_MODALITY_VIDEO: video - MODEL_MODALITY_EMBEDDING: embedding vectors - MODEL_MODALITY_RANKING: document ranking scores produced by reranking models - MODEL_MODALITY_DECISIONS: structured decisions produced by classification models
---@field output_modality? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestOutputModalityList Require every listed modality as a model output. Multiple values use AND semantics. - MODEL_MODALITY_TEXT: plain text - MODEL_MODALITY_IMAGE: still images - MODEL_MODALITY_AUDIO: audio - MODEL_MODALITY_VIDEO: video - MODEL_MODALITY_EMBEDDING: embedding vectors - MODEL_MODALITY_RANKING: document ranking scores produced by reranking models - MODEL_MODALITY_DECISIONS: structured decisions produced by classification models
---@field product? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestProductList Filter by product enrollment. - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATIONS_JUDGE: Model can judge evaluations. - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_HARNESS_RUNTIME: Model is enrolled for the harness runtime. - MODEL_CATALOG_PRODUCT_EVALUATION_CANDIDATE: Model can be an evaluation or simulation candidate. It serves a text endpoint and accepts and returns text.
---@field capabilities? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestCapabilitiesList Require every listed capability. Multiple values use AND semantics. `coding` matches a coding specialisation, not only models whose type is coding.
---@field item_type? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestItemTypeList Include foundation models, Inference Router presets, or both. Omit to return both. - MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_MODEL: A foundation or inference model. - MODEL_CATALOG_ITEM_TYPE_INFERENCE_ROUTER: An Inference Router preset.
---@field sort_by? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestSortBy|string Field to sort results by. Default is `MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT`. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_CREATED_AT: Sort by creation date. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_NAME: Sort by display name, case-insensitive. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_PRICE: Sort by input token price. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_E2E_LATENCY_P50: Sort by canary end-to-end latency p50, in seconds. Lower is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_THROUGHPUT_P50: Sort by canary throughput p50, in tokens per second. Higher is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data. - MODEL_CATALOG_SORT_BY_TTFT_P50: Sort by canary time to first token p50, in seconds. Lower is better. Rows without performance data sort after rows with data.
---@field sort_direction? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestSortDirection|string Sort direction. Defaults to descending when unspecified.
---@field creator? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiModelCatalogV2RequestCreatorList Filter by model creator or developer, such as Meta or Google. Multiple values use OR semantics and match case-insensitively. Use `available_creators` in the response to discover valid options.

