---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiSimulationEpisodesRequest
---@field run_uuid string UUID of the run whose episodes to list.
---@field scenario_uuid? string Optional filter by scenario.
---@field page? number Page number.
---@field per_page? number Items per page.
---@field statuses? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiSimulationEpisodesRequestStatusesList Filter by one or more statuses. Empty means no status filter. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_STATUS_RUNNING: The episode is executing and a trajectory is available to retrieve. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_STATUS_FINISHED: The episode reached a stop condition and produced a verdict. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_STATUS_FAILED: The episode failed because of a cancel, timeout, or error. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_STATUS_PREPARING: The episode is allocated but its trajectory is not available yet.
---@field verdicts? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiSimulationEpisodesRequestVerdictsList Filter by one or more verdicts. Empty means no verdict filter. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_VERDICT_SUCCESS: The candidate agent satisfied the scenario's stopping criteria. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_VERDICT_FAILURE: The candidate agent did not satisfy the stopping criteria. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_VERDICT_INCONCLUSIVE: No conclusive verdict (e.g. max_turns reached without the judge finishing).
---@field search? string Free-text search across scenario_uuid and session_id (case-insensitive substring match). Empty means no search.
---@field sort_by? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiSimulationEpisodesRequestSortBy|string Field to sort by. Defaults to scenario ordering when unspecified. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_SORT_FIELD_SCENARIO: Sort by scenario_uuid then episode_index. Default. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_SORT_FIELD_CREATED_AT: Sort by creation date. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_SORT_FIELD_STATUS: Sort by episode status using lifecycle order. - SIMULATION_EPISODE_SORT_FIELD_VERDICT: Sort by verdict (nulls last).
---@field sort_direction? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListGenaiSimulationEpisodesRequestSortDirection|string Sort direction. Defaults to ascending when unspecified.

