---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessSessionsRequest
---@field page_size? number Page size. Defaults to 50 when omitted or non-positive; values above 200 are clamped to 200 (not rejected).
---@field page_token? string Opaque keyset cursor returned by the previous page. Empty starts from the beginning.
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.SessionStatus|string Optional filter on session status. Empty / SESSION_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED means no explicit filter, which still hides destroyed and failed sessions by default; SESSION_STATUS_ALL opts out and returns every session regardless of status (no session is ever actually in this status; it only means something as a filter value here); any other explicit status overrides the default.
---@field name? string Optional exact-name filter (case-insensitive). Returns the single live (non-terminal) session that currently holds this name for the caller's team, or an empty list if none does. Matches the live holder only, so historical terminal rows and reused names never make it ambiguous (per-team live-name uniqueness bounds it to at most one). This is how clients (doctl / Console) resolve a session name to its id; the {session_id} path stays UUID-only.
---@field search? string Optional case-insensitive substring filter on session name (contains), for callers that don't know the exact name (e.g. a UI search box). Unlike `name`, this may return zero, one, or many sessions, including terminal ones. Independent of `name`; at most 64 characters.

