---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancer
---@field id string A unique ID that can be used to identify and reference a load balancer.
---@field name string A human-readable name for a load balancer instance.
---@field project_id? string The ID of the project that the load balancer is associated with. If no ID is provided at creation, the load balancer associates with the user's default project. If an invalid project ID is provided, the load balancer will not be created.
---@field ipv6? string An attribute containing the public-facing IPv6 address of the load balancer.
---@field size_unit? number How many nodes the load balancer contains. Each additional node increases the load balancer's ability to manage more connections. Load balancers can be scaled up or down, and you can change the number of nodes after creation up to once per hour. This field is currently not available in the AMS2, NYC2, or SFO1 regions. Use the `size` field to scale load balancers that reside in these regions.
---@field size? digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerSize This field has been replaced by the `size_unit` field for all regions except in AMS2, NYC2, and SFO1. Each available load balancer size now equates to the load balancer having a set number of nodes. * `lb-small` = 1 node * `lb-medium` = 3 nodes * `lb-large` = 6 nodes You can resize load balancers after creation up to once per hour. You cannot resize a load balancer within the first hour of its creation.
---@field algorithm? digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerAlgorithm This field has been deprecated. You can no longer specify an algorithm for load balancers.
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerStatus A status string indicating the current state of the load balancer. This can be `new`, `active`, or `errored`.
---@field created_at string A time value given in ISO8601 combined date and time format that represents when the load balancer was created.
---@field forwarding_rules digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerForwardingRulesList An array of objects specifying the forwarding rules for a load balancer.
---@field health_check? digitalocean.digitalocean.HealthCheck
---@field sticky_sessions? digitalocean.digitalocean.StickySessions
---@field redirect_http_to_https? boolean A boolean value indicating whether HTTP requests to the load balancer on port 80 will be redirected to HTTPS on port 443.
---@field enable_proxy_protocol? boolean A boolean value indicating whether PROXY Protocol is in use.
---@field enable_backend_keepalive? boolean A boolean value indicating whether HTTP keepalive connections are maintained to target Droplets.
---@field http_idle_timeout_seconds? number An integer value which configures the idle timeout for HTTP requests to the target droplets.
---@field vpc_uuid? string A string specifying the UUID of the VPC to which the load balancer is assigned.
---@field subnet_uuid? string A string specifying the UUID of the VPC subnet to which the load balancer is assigned.
---@field disable_lets_encrypt_dns_records? boolean A boolean value indicating whether to disable automatic DNS record creation for Let's Encrypt certificates that are added to the load balancer.
---@field firewall? digitalocean.digitalocean.LbFirewall
---@field network? digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerNetwork A string indicating whether the load balancer should be external or internal. Internal load balancers have no public IPs and are only accessible to resources on the same VPC network. This property cannot be updated after creating the load balancer.
---@field network_stack? digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerNetworkStack A string indicating whether the load balancer will support IPv4 or both IPv4 and IPv6 networking. This property cannot be updated after creating the load balancer.
---@field type? digitalocean.digitalocean.LoadBalancerType A string indicating whether the load balancer should be a standard regional HTTP load balancer, a regional network load balancer that routes traffic at the TCP/UDP transport layer, or a global load balancer.
