---MCP server registered by your team. It never contains secret material.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServer
---@field serverRef string Server identifier, unique within your team. The server's tool slugs are `<server_ref>_<name>`.
---@field endpoint string HTTPS URL of the server's MCP endpoint.
---@field transport? digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerTransport Always `streamable_http`.
---@field credentialRefSource? digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerCredentialRefSource How requests to the server authenticate: none, secret (a key or token sent in the Authorization header), or connection (each user's own OAuth authorization).
---@field credentialRef? string The secret reference supplied at registration when source=secret, or the team's OAuth credential ID when source=connection. Empty when the server was registered with an `api_key`, whose storage DigitalOcean manages.
---@field syncStatus? digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerSyncStatus Outcome of the latest discovery: pending (no discovery has finished yet), ok, failed, or `unsupported_protocol`. It is not reset while a resync runs.
---@field syncError? string Why the latest discovery failed; empty after a successful one.
---@field lastSyncedAt? string When discovery last succeeded, in RFC 3339 format; empty until the first success.
---@field protocolVersion? string MCP protocol revision negotiated with the server.
---@field toolCount? number Number of tools discovered on the server, whether enabled or not.
---@field createdAt? string When the server was registered, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field updatedAt? string When the server was last modified, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field description? string Team-authored description, shown on the server's catalog card. A resync does not replace it.
---@field oauth_authorize_url? string OAuth authorization endpoint. Set only when `credentialRefSource` is connection; the client secret is never returned.
---@field oauth_scopes? digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerOauthScopesList OAuth scopes requested from each user. Set only when `credentialRefSource` is connection.
---@field oauth_authorization_ttl_seconds? string How long a user's authorization is reused before re-consent. Echoed so a team can read the window without re-registering to discover it.

---How requests to the server authenticate: none, secret (a key or token sent in the Authorization header), or connection (each user's own OAuth authorization).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerCredentialRefSource "none"|"secret"|"connection"

---OAuth scopes requested from each user. Set only when `credentialRefSource` is connection.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerOauthScopesList string[]

---Returns one MCP server.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerResponse
---@field mcpServer digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServer The MCP server.

---Outcome of the latest discovery: pending (no discovery has finished yet), ok, failed, or `unsupported_protocol`. It is not reset while a resync runs.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerSyncStatus "pending"|"ok"|"failed"|"unsupported_protocol"

