---@field ["end"] string UNIX timestamp to end metric window.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfig
---@field backup_hour? number The hour of day (in UTC) when backup for the service starts. New backup only starts if previous backup has already completed.
---@field backup_minute? number The minute of the backup hour when backup for the service starts. New backup only starts if previous backup has already completed.
---@field automatic_sp_privileges? boolean When enabled, grants `EXECUTE` and `ALTER ROUTINE` privileges to the creator of a stored routine. When disabled, these privileges are not granted automatically.
---@field sql_mode? string Global SQL mode. If empty, uses MySQL server defaults. Must only include uppercase alphabetic characters, underscores, and commas.
---@field connect_timeout? number The number of seconds that the mysqld server waits for a connect packet before responding with bad handshake.
---@field default_time_zone? string Default server time zone, in the form of an offset from UTC (from -12:00 to +12:00), a time zone name (EST), or 'SYSTEM' to use the MySQL server default.
---@field div_precision_increment? number The number of digits by which to increase the scale of the result of division operations performed with the `/` operator.
---@field end_markers_in_json? boolean When enabled, the JSON output of `EXPLAIN FORMAT=JSON` includes end markers for nested structures.
---@field eq_range_index_dive_limit? number The number of equality ranges in an equality comparison condition when the optimizer should switch from using index dives to index statistics.
---@field group_concat_max_len? number The maximum permitted result length, in bytes, for the GROUP_CONCAT() function.
---@field information_schema_stats_expiry? number The time, in seconds, before cached statistics expire.
---@field innodb_adaptive_hash_index? boolean When enabled, InnoDB uses an adaptive hash index to speed up equality lookups. The optimal setting is workload-dependent: it can improve performance for some workloads, but under high concurrency the associated latch can become a contention point, in which case disabling it may improve throughput. Default is true.
---@field innodb_ft_enable_stopword? boolean When enabled, the InnoDB FULLTEXT index stopword list is used. Disabled by default when a custom stopword table is configured.
---@field innodb_ft_max_token_size? number The maximum length of words that an InnoDB FULLTEXT index stores. Changing this parameter will lead to a restart of the MySQL service.
---@field innodb_ft_min_token_size? number The minimum length of words that an InnoDB FULLTEXT index stores.
---@field innodb_ft_num_word_optimize? number The number of words to process during each OPTIMIZE TABLE operation on an InnoDB FULLTEXT index.
---@field innodb_ft_result_cache_limit? number The InnoDB FULLTEXT index query result cache size limit, in bytes.
---@field innodb_ft_server_stopword_table? string The InnoDB FULLTEXT index stopword list for all InnoDB tables.
---@field innodb_ft_user_stopword_table? string|distilled.Null The InnoDB FULLTEXT index stopword list for user-created FULLTEXT indexes. Must be in the form `db_name/table_name`. Set to `null` to clear a previously configured value.
---@field innodb_lock_wait_timeout? number The time, in seconds, that an InnoDB transaction waits for a row lock. before giving up.
---@field innodb_log_buffer_size? number The size of the buffer, in bytes, that InnoDB uses to write to the log files. on disk.
---@field innodb_online_alter_log_max_size? number The upper limit, in bytes, of the size of the temporary log files used during online DDL operations for InnoDB tables.
---@field innodb_optimize_fulltext_only? boolean When enabled, OPTIMIZE TABLE rebuilds only the InnoDB FULLTEXT index, not the table itself.
---@field innodb_print_all_deadlocks? boolean When enabled, records information about all deadlocks in InnoDB user transactions in the error log. Disabled by default.
---@field innodb_rollback_on_timeout? boolean When enabled, transaction timeouts cause InnoDB to abort and roll back the entire transaction.
---@field interactive_timeout? number The time, in seconds, the server waits for activity on an interactive. connection before closing it.
---@field internal_tmp_mem_storage_engine? digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigInternalTmpMemStorageEngine|string The storage engine for in-memory internal temporary tables.
---@field net_read_timeout? number The time, in seconds, to wait for more data from an existing connection. aborting the read.
---@field net_write_timeout? number The number of seconds to wait for a block to be written to a connection before aborting the write.
---@field sql_require_primary_key? boolean Require primary key to be defined for new tables or old tables modified with ALTER TABLE and fail if missing. It is recommended to always have primary keys because various functionality may break if any large table is missing them.
---@field wait_timeout? number The number of seconds the server waits for activity on a noninteractive connection before closing it.
---@field windowing_use_high_precision? boolean When enabled, window functions use a higher precision for internal calculations, which can be more accurate but slower.
---@field max_allowed_packet? number The size of the largest message, in bytes, that can be received by the server. Default is 67108864 (64M).
---@field max_execution_time? number The execution timeout for `SELECT` statements, in milliseconds. A value of `0` disables the timeout (no limit).
---@field max_heap_table_size? number The maximum size, in bytes, of internal in-memory tables. Also set tmp_table_size. Default is 16777216 (16M)
---@field max_seeks_for_key? number Limits the assumed maximum number of seeks when looking up rows based on a key. Lower values cause the query optimizer to prefer indexes over table scans for non-covering indexes.
---@field optimizer_prune_level? number Controls the heuristics applied during query optimization to prune less promising partial plans from the optimizer search space. `0` disables pruning and `1` enables it.
---@field optimizer_search_depth? number The maximum depth of search performed by the query optimizer. Smaller values can reduce compilation time for large joins; a value of `0` lets the server automatically pick a reasonable value.
---@field optimizer_switch? string Controls query optimizer behavior as a comma-separated list of `option=value` pairs, or `default` to restore server defaults. Each value must be `on`, `off`, or `default`.
---@field sort_buffer_size? number The sort buffer size, in bytes, for ORDER BY optimization. Default is 262144. (256K).
---@field tmp_table_size? number The maximum size, in bytes, of internal in-memory tables. Also set max_heap_table_size. Default is 16777216 (16M).
---@field slow_query_log? boolean When enabled, captures slow queries. When disabled, also truncates the mysql.slow_log table. Default is false.
---@field long_query_time? number The time, in seconds, for a query to take to execute before being captured by slow_query_logs. Default is 10 seconds.
---@field binlog_retention_period? number The minimum amount of time, in seconds, to keep binlog entries before deletion. This may be extended for services that require binlog entries for longer than the default, for example if using the MySQL Debezium Kafka connector.
---@field innodb_change_buffer_max_size? number Specifies the maximum size of the InnoDB change buffer as a percentage of the buffer pool.
---@field innodb_flush_neighbors? digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigInnodbFlushNeighbors|number Specifies whether flushing a page from the InnoDB buffer pool also flushes other dirty pages in the same extent. - 0 &mdash; disables this functionality, dirty pages in the same extent are not flushed. - 1 &mdash; flushes contiguous dirty pages in the same extent. - 2 &mdash; flushes dirty pages in the same extent.
---@field innodb_read_io_threads? number The number of I/O threads for read operations in InnoDB. Changing this parameter will lead to a restart of the MySQL service.
---@field innodb_write_io_threads? number The number of I/O threads for write operations in InnoDB. Changing this parameter will lead to a restart of the MySQL service.
---@field innodb_thread_concurrency? number Defines the maximum number of threads permitted inside of InnoDB. A value of 0 (the default) is interpreted as infinite concurrency (no limit). This variable is intended for performance tuning on high concurrency systems.
---@field net_buffer_length? number Start sizes of connection buffer and result buffer, must be multiple of 1024. Changing this parameter will lead to a restart of the MySQL service.
---@field log_output? digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigLogOutput|string Defines the destination for logs. Can be `INSIGHTS`, `TABLE`, or both (`INSIGHTS,TABLE`), or `NONE` to disable logs. To specify both destinations, use `INSIGHTS,TABLE` (order matters). Default is NONE.
---@field mysql_incremental_backup? digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlIncrementalBackup

---Specifies whether flushing a page from the InnoDB buffer pool also flushes other dirty pages in the same extent.
---  - 0 &mdash; disables this functionality, dirty pages in the same extent are not flushed.
---  - 1 &mdash; flushes contiguous dirty pages in the same extent.
---  - 2 &mdash; flushes dirty pages in the same extent.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigInnodbFlushNeighbors 0|1|2

---The storage engine for in-memory internal temporary tables.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigInternalTmpMemStorageEngine "TempTable"|"MEMORY"

---Defines the destination for logs. Can be `INSIGHTS`, `TABLE`, or both (`INSIGHTS,TABLE`), or `NONE` to disable logs. To specify both destinations, use `INSIGHTS,TABLE` (order matters). Default is NONE.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlAdvancedConfigLogOutput "INSIGHTS"|"TABLE"|"INSIGHTS,TABLE"|"NONE"

---MySQL Incremental Backup configuration settings
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlIncrementalBackup
---@field enabled? boolean Enable periodic incremental backups. When enabled, full_backup_week_schedule must be set. Incremental backups only store changes since the last backup, making them faster and more storage-efficient than full backups. This is particularly useful for large databases where daily full backups would be too time-consuming or expensive.
---@field full_backup_week_schedule? string Comma-separated list of days of the week when full backups should be created. Valid values: mon, tue, wed, thu, fri, sat, sun. Default is null. Example : "mon,fri,sun".

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlSettings
---@field auth_plugin digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlSettingsAuthPlugin|string A string specifying the authentication method to be used for connections to the MySQL user account. The valid values are `mysql_native_password` or `caching_sha2_password`. If excluded when creating a new user, the default for the version of MySQL in use will be used. As of MySQL 8.0, the default is `caching_sha2_password`.

---A string specifying the authentication method to be used for connections
---to the MySQL user account. The valid values are `mysql_native_password`
---or `caching_sha2_password`. If excluded when creating a new user, the
---default for the version of MySQL in use will be used. As of MySQL 8.0, the
---default is `caching_sha2_password`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.MysqlSettingsAuthPlugin "mysql_native_password"|"caching_sha2_password"

