---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.OpensearchAdvancedConfig
---@field http_max_content_length_bytes? number Maximum content length for HTTP requests to the OpenSearch HTTP API, in bytes.
---@field http_max_header_size_bytes? number Maximum size of allowed headers, in bytes.
---@field http_max_initial_line_length_bytes? number Maximum length of an HTTP URL, in bytes.
---@field indices_query_bool_max_clause_count? number Maximum number of clauses Lucene BooleanQuery can have. Only increase it if necessary, as it may cause performance issues.
---@field indices_fielddata_cache_size_percentage? number Maximum amount of heap memory used for field data cache, expressed as a percentage. Decreasing the value too much will increase overhead of loading field data. Increasing the value too much will decrease amount of heap available for other operations.
---@field indices_memory_index_buffer_size_percentage? number Total amount of heap used for indexing buffer before writing segments to disk, expressed as a percentage. Too low value will slow down indexing; too high value will increase indexing performance but causes performance issues for query performance.
---@field indices_memory_min_index_buffer_size_mb? number Minimum amount of heap used for indexing buffer before writing segments to disk, in mb. Works in conjunction with indices_memory_index_buffer_size_percentage, each being enforced.
---@field indices_memory_max_index_buffer_size_mb? number Maximum amount of heap used for indexing buffer before writing segments to disk, in mb. Works in conjunction with indices_memory_index_buffer_size_percentage, each being enforced. The default is unbounded.
---@field indices_queries_cache_size_percentage? number Maximum amount of heap used for query cache. Too low value will decrease query performance and increase performance for other operations; too high value will cause issues with other functionality.
---@field indices_recovery_max_mb_per_sec? number Limits total inbound and outbound recovery traffic for each node, expressed in mb per second. Applies to both peer recoveries as well as snapshot recoveries (i.e., restores from a snapshot).
---@field indices_recovery_max_concurrent_file_chunks? number Maximum number of file chunks sent in parallel for each recovery.
---@field thread_pool_search_size? number Number of workers in the search operation thread pool. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_search_throttled_size? number Number of workers in the search throttled operation thread pool. This pool is used for searching frozen indices. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_get_size? number Number of workers in the get operation thread pool. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_analyze_size? number Number of workers in the analyze operation thread pool. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_write_size? number Number of workers in the write operation thread pool. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_force_merge_size? number Number of workers in the force merge operation thread pool. This pool is used for forcing a merge between shards of one or more indices. Do note this may have maximum value depending on CPU count - value is automatically lowered if set to higher than maximum value.
---@field thread_pool_search_queue_size? number Size of queue for operations in the search thread pool.
---@field thread_pool_search_throttled_queue_size? number Size of queue for operations in the search throttled thread pool.
---@field thread_pool_get_queue_size? number Size of queue for operations in the get thread pool.
---@field thread_pool_analyze_queue_size? number Size of queue for operations in the analyze thread pool.
---@field thread_pool_write_queue_size? number Size of queue for operations in the write thread pool.
---@field ism_enabled? boolean Specifies whether ISM is enabled or not.
---@field ism_history_enabled? boolean Specifies whether audit history is enabled or not. The logs from ISM are automatically indexed to a logs document.
---@field ism_history_max_age_hours? number Maximum age before rolling over the audit history index, in hours.
---@field ism_history_max_docs? number Maximum number of documents before rolling over the audit history index.
---@field ism_history_rollover_check_period_hours? number The time between rollover checks for the audit history index, in hours.
---@field ism_history_rollover_retention_period_days? number Length of time long audit history indices are kept, in days.
---@field search_max_buckets? number Maximum number of aggregation buckets allowed in a single response.
---@field action_auto_create_index_enabled? boolean Specifices whether to allow automatic creation of indices.
---@field enable_security_audit? boolean Specifies whether to allow security audit logging.
---@field action_destructive_requires_name? boolean Specifies whether to require explicit index names when deleting indices.
---@field cluster_max_shards_per_node? number Maximum number of shards allowed per data node.
---@field override_main_response_version? boolean Compatibility mode sets OpenSearch to report its version as 7.10 so clients continue to work.
---@field script_max_compilations_rate? string Limits the number of inline script compilations within a period of time. Default is use-context
---@field cluster_routing_allocation_node_concurrent_recoveries? number Maximum concurrent incoming/outgoing shard recoveries (normally replicas) are allowed to happen per node .
---@field reindex_remote_whitelist? digitalocean.digitalocean.OpensearchAdvancedConfigReindexRemoteWhitelistList Allowlist of remote IP addresses for reindexing. Changing this value will cause all OpenSearch instances to restart.
---@field plugins_alerting_filter_by_backend_roles_enabled? boolean Enable or disable filtering of alerting by backend roles.
---@field knn_memory_circuit_breaker_enabled? boolean Enable or disable KNN memory circuit breaker.
---@field knn_memory_circuit_breaker_limit? number Maximum amount of memory in percentage that can be used for the KNN index. Defaults to 50% of the JVM heap size. 0 is used to set it to null which can be used to invalidate caches.
---@field keep_index_refresh_interval? boolean DigitalOcean automatically resets the `index.refresh_interval` to the default value (once per second) to ensure that new documents are quickly available for search queries. If you are setting your own refresh intervals, you can disable this by setting this field to true.

---Allowlist of remote IP addresses for reindexing. Changing this value will cause all OpenSearch instances to restart.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.OpensearchAdvancedConfigReindexRemoteWhitelistList string[]

