---PGBouncer connection pooling settings
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfig
---@field server_reset_query_always? boolean Run server_reset_query (DISCARD ALL) in all pooling modes.
---@field ignore_startup_parameters? digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigIgnoreStartupParametersList List of parameters to ignore when given in startup packet.
---@field min_pool_size? number If current server connections are below this number, adds more. Improves behavior when usual load comes suddenly back after period of total inactivity. The value is effectively capped at the pool size.
---@field server_lifetime? number The pooler closes any unused server connection that has been connected longer than this amount of seconds.
---@field server_idle_timeout? number Drops server connections if they have been idle more than this many seconds. If 0, timeout is disabled.
---@field autodb_pool_size? number If non-zero, automatically creates a pool of that size per user when a pool doesn't exist.
---@field autodb_pool_mode? digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigAutodbPoolMode|string PGBouncer pool mode
---@field autodb_max_db_connections? number Only allows a maximum this many server connections per database (regardless of user). If 0, allows unlimited connections.
---@field autodb_idle_timeout? number If the automatically-created database pools have been unused this many seconds, they are freed. If 0, timeout is disabled.

---PGBouncer pool mode
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigAutodbPoolMode "session"|"transaction"|"statement"

---Enum of parameters to ignore when given in startup packet.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigIgnoreStartupParametersItem "extra_float_digits"|"search_path"

---List of parameters to ignore when given in startup packet.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigIgnoreStartupParametersList (digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfigIgnoreStartupParametersItem|string)[]

