---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfig
---@field autovacuum_freeze_max_age? number Specifies the maximum age (in transactions) that a table's pg_class.relfrozenxid field can attain before a VACUUM operation is forced to prevent transaction ID wraparound within the table. Note that the system will launch autovacuum processes to prevent wraparound even when autovacuum is otherwise disabled. This parameter will cause the server to be restarted.
---@field autovacuum_max_workers? number Specifies the maximum number of autovacuum processes (other than the autovacuum launcher) that may be running at any one time. The default is three. This parameter can only be set at server start.
---@field autovacuum_naptime? number Specifies the minimum delay, in seconds, between autovacuum runs on any given database. The default is one minute.
---@field autovacuum_vacuum_threshold? number Specifies the minimum number of updated or deleted tuples needed to trigger a VACUUM in any one table. The default is 50 tuples.
---@field autovacuum_analyze_threshold? number Specifies the minimum number of inserted, updated, or deleted tuples needed to trigger an ANALYZE in any one table. The default is 50 tuples.
---@field autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor? number Specifies a fraction, in a decimal value, of the table size to add to autovacuum_vacuum_threshold when deciding whether to trigger a VACUUM. The default is 0.2 (20% of table size).
---@field autovacuum_analyze_scale_factor? number Specifies a fraction, in a decimal value, of the table size to add to autovacuum_analyze_threshold when deciding whether to trigger an ANALYZE. The default is 0.2 (20% of table size).
---@field autovacuum_vacuum_cost_delay? number Specifies the cost delay value, in milliseconds, that will be used in automatic VACUUM operations. If -1, uses the regular vacuum_cost_delay value, which is 20 milliseconds.
---@field autovacuum_vacuum_cost_limit? number Specifies the cost limit value that will be used in automatic VACUUM operations. If -1 is specified (which is the default), the regular vacuum_cost_limit value will be used.
---@field backup_hour? number The hour of day (in UTC) when backup for the service starts. New backup only starts if previous backup has already completed.
---@field backup_minute? number The minute of the backup hour when backup for the service starts. New backup is only started if previous backup has already completed.
---@field bgwriter_delay? number Specifies the delay, in milliseconds, between activity rounds for the background writer. Default is 200 ms.
---@field bgwriter_flush_after? number The amount of kilobytes that need to be written by the background writer before attempting to force the OS to issue these writes to underlying storage. Specified in kilobytes, default is 512. Setting of 0 disables forced writeback.
---@field bgwriter_lru_maxpages? number The maximum number of buffers that the background writer can write. Setting this to zero disables background writing. Default is 100.
---@field bgwriter_lru_multiplier? number The average recent need for new buffers is multiplied by bgwriter_lru_multiplier to arrive at an estimate of the number that will be needed during the next round, (up to bgwriter_lru_maxpages). 1.0 represents a “just in time” policy of writing exactly the number of buffers predicted to be needed. Larger values provide some cushion against spikes in demand, while smaller values intentionally leave writes to be done by server processes. The default is 2.0.
---@field deadlock_timeout? number The amount of time, in milliseconds, to wait on a lock before checking to see if there is a deadlock condition.
---@field default_toast_compression? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigDefaultToastCompression|string Specifies the default TOAST compression method for values of compressible columns (the default is lz4).
---@field idle_in_transaction_session_timeout? number Time out sessions with open transactions after this number of milliseconds
---@field jit? boolean Activates, in a boolean, the system-wide use of Just-in-Time Compilation (JIT).
---@field log_autovacuum_min_duration? number Causes each action executed by autovacuum to be logged if it ran for at least the specified number of milliseconds. Setting this to zero logs all autovacuum actions. Minus-one (the default) disables logging autovacuum actions.
---@field log_error_verbosity? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigLogErrorVerbosity|string Controls the amount of detail written in the server log for each message that is logged.
---@field log_line_prefix? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigLogLinePrefix|string Selects one of the available log-formats. These can support popular log analyzers like pgbadger, pganalyze, etc.
---@field log_min_duration_statement? number Log statements that take more than this number of milliseconds to run. If -1, disables.
---@field max_files_per_process? number PostgreSQL maximum number of files that can be open per process.
---@field max_prepared_transactions? number PostgreSQL maximum prepared transactions. Once increased, this parameter cannot be lowered from its set value.
---@field max_pred_locks_per_transaction? number PostgreSQL maximum predicate locks per transaction.
---@field max_locks_per_transaction? number PostgreSQL maximum locks per transaction. Once increased, this parameter cannot be lowered from its set value.
---@field max_stack_depth? number Maximum depth of the stack in bytes.
---@field max_standby_archive_delay? number Max standby archive delay in milliseconds.
---@field max_standby_streaming_delay? number Max standby streaming delay in milliseconds.
---@field max_replication_slots? number PostgreSQL maximum replication slots.
---@field max_logical_replication_workers? number PostgreSQL maximum logical replication workers (taken from the pool of max_parallel_workers).
---@field max_parallel_workers? number Sets the maximum number of workers that the system can support for parallel queries.
---@field max_parallel_workers_per_gather? number Sets the maximum number of workers that can be started by a single Gather or Gather Merge node.
---@field max_worker_processes? number Sets the maximum number of background processes that the system can support. Once increased, this parameter cannot be lowered from its set value.
---@field pg_partman_bgw_role? string Controls which role to use for pg_partman's scheduled background tasks. Must consist of alpha-numeric characters, dots, underscores, or dashes. May not start with dash or dot. Maximum of 64 characters.
---@field pg_partman_bgw_interval? number Sets the time interval to run pg_partman's scheduled tasks.
---@field pg_stat_statements_track? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgStatStatementsTrack|string Controls which statements are counted. Specify 'top' to track top-level statements (those issued directly by clients), 'all' to also track nested statements (such as statements invoked within functions), or 'none' to disable statement statistics collection. The default value is top.
---@field temp_file_limit? number PostgreSQL temporary file limit in KiB. If -1, sets to unlimited.
---@field timezone? string PostgreSQL service timezone
---@field track_activity_query_size? number Specifies the number of bytes reserved to track the currently executing command for each active session.
---@field track_commit_timestamp? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackCommitTimestamp|string Record commit time of transactions.
---@field track_functions? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackFunctions|string Enables tracking of function call counts and time used.
---@field track_io_timing? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackIoTiming|string Enables timing of database I/O calls. This parameter is off by default, because it will repeatedly query the operating system for the current time, which may cause significant overhead on some platforms.
---@field max_wal_senders? number PostgreSQL maximum WAL senders. Once increased, this parameter cannot be lowered from its set value.
---@field wal_sender_timeout? number Terminate replication connections that are inactive for longer than this amount of time, in milliseconds. Setting this value to zero disables the timeout. Must be either 0 or between 5000 and 10800000.
---@field wal_writer_delay? number WAL flush interval in milliseconds. Note that setting this value to lower than the default 200ms may negatively impact performance
---@field shared_buffers_percentage? number Percentage of total RAM that the database server uses for shared memory buffers. Valid range is 20-60 (float), which corresponds to 20% - 60%. This setting adjusts the shared_buffers configuration value.
---@field pgbouncer? digitalocean.digitalocean.PgbouncerAdvancedConfig
---@field work_mem? number The maximum amount of memory, in MB, used by a query operation (such as a sort or hash table) before writing to temporary disk files. Default is 1MB + 0.075% of total RAM (up to 32MB).
---@field timescaledb? digitalocean.digitalocean.TimescaledbAdvancedConfig
---@field synchronous_replication? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigSynchronousReplication|string Synchronous replication type. Note that the service plan also needs to support synchronous replication.
---@field stat_monitor_enable? boolean Enable the pg_stat_monitor extension. <b>Enabling this extension will cause the cluster to be restarted.</b> When this extension is enabled, pg_stat_statements results for utility commands are unreliable.
---@field max_failover_replication_time_lag? number Number of seconds of master unavailability before triggering database failover to standby. The default value is 60.
---@field max_connections? number Sets the PostgreSQL maximum number of concurrent connections to the database server. This is a limited-release parameter. Contact your account team to confirm your eligibility. You cannot decrease this parameter value when set. For services with a read replica, first increase the read replica's value. After the change is applied to the replica, you can increase the primary service's value. Changing this parameter causes a service restart.
---@field max_slot_wal_keep_size? number PostgreSQL maximum WAL size (MB) reserved for replication slots. If -1 is specified, replication slots may retain an unlimited amount of WAL files. The default is -1 (upstream default). wal_keep_size minimum WAL size setting takes precedence over this.
---@field pgaudit? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgaudit System-wide settings for the pgaudit extension. When `feature_enabled` is true, the pgaudit extension is automatically installed. When false, the extension is uninstalled but auditing configurations (such as `log`) are preserved.

---Specifies the default TOAST compression method for values of compressible columns (the default is lz4).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigDefaultToastCompression "lz4"|"pglz"

---Controls the amount of detail written in the server log for each message that is logged.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigLogErrorVerbosity "TERSE"|"DEFAULT"|"VERBOSE"

---Selects one of the available log-formats. These can support popular log analyzers like pgbadger, pganalyze, etc.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigLogLinePrefix "pid=%p,user=%u,db=%d,app=%a,client=%h"|"%m [%p] %q[user=%u,db=%d,app=%a]"|"%t [%p]: [%l-1] user=%u,db=%d,app=%a,client=%h"

---Controls which statements are counted. Specify 'top' to track top-level statements (those issued directly by clients), 'all' to also track nested statements (such as statements invoked within functions), or 'none' to disable statement statistics collection. The default value is top.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgStatStatementsTrack "all"|"top"|"none"

---System-wide settings for the pgaudit extension. When `feature_enabled` is true, the pgaudit extension is automatically installed. When false, the extension is uninstalled but auditing configurations (such as `log`) are preserved.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgaudit
---@field feature_enabled? boolean Enable pgaudit extension. When enabled, pgaudit extension will be automatically installed. Otherwise, extension will be uninstalled but auditing configurations will be preserved.
---@field log? digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgauditLogList Specifies which classes of statements will be logged by session audit logging. Available values are `read` (SELECT and COPY when the source is a relation or query), `write` (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, TRUNCATE, and COPY when the destination is a relation), `function` (function calls and DO blocks), `role` (statements related to roles and privileges: GRANT, REVOKE, CREATE/ALTER/DROP ROLE), `ddl` (all DDL that is not included in the role class), `misc` (miscellaneous commands, e.g. DISCARD, FETCH, CHECKPOINT, VACUUM, SET), `misc_set` (miscellaneous SET commands, e.g. SET ROLE), and `all` (include all of the above).

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgauditLogItem "read"|"write"|"function"|"role"|"ddl"|"misc"|"misc_set"|"all"

---Specifies which classes of statements will be logged by session audit logging. Available values are `read` (SELECT and COPY when the source is a relation or query), `write` (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, TRUNCATE, and COPY when the destination is a relation), `function` (function calls and DO blocks), `role` (statements related to roles and privileges: GRANT, REVOKE, CREATE/ALTER/DROP ROLE), `ddl` (all DDL that is not included in the role class), `misc` (miscellaneous commands, e.g. DISCARD, FETCH, CHECKPOINT, VACUUM, SET), `misc_set` (miscellaneous SET commands, e.g. SET ROLE), and `all` (include all of the above).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgauditLogList (digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigPgauditLogItem|string)[]

---Synchronous replication type. Note that the service plan also needs to support synchronous replication.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigSynchronousReplication "off"|"quorum"

---Record commit time of transactions.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackCommitTimestamp "off"|"on"

---Enables tracking of function call counts and time used.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackFunctions "all"|"pl"|"none"

---Enables timing of database I/O calls. This parameter is off by default, because it will repeatedly query the operating system for the current time, which may cause significant overhead on some platforms.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.PostgresAdvancedConfigTrackIoTiming "off"|"on"

