---Describes a catalog provider and how to authenticate to it.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummary
---@field name? string Provider slug, used as provider when creating a connection or a provider credential.
---@field display_name? string Human-readable provider name.
---@field description? string Provider description.
---@field auth_types? digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryAuthTypesList Credential kinds the provider accepts, sorted: none|oauth|`shared_api_key`|unknown|`user_oauth_app`|`user_token`. `none` means the provider needs no credential. `oauth` means users can connect through DigitalOcean's shared OAuth application. `user_oauth_app` means users can connect through an OAuth client your team registers as a provider credential; without `oauth` alongside it, that is the only way to connect. `shared_api_key` means DigitalOcean supplies the key. `user_token` means your team or its users supply a key or token. `unknown` means the provider declares no kind this API recognizes, including an OAuth provider whose shared application is not available. It is never paired with another kind.
---@field auth_type? string Deprecated: read `auth_types`, since a provider may accept more than one credential kind. This is the first entry of `auth_types` other than `none`, or `none` when that is the only entry.
---@field scopes? digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryScopesList The OAuth scopes a connection may request; a connection that requests none gets all of them. Set only when `auth_types` contains `oauth` or `user_oauth_app`.
---@field connection_parameters? digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryConnectionParametersList Non-sensitive values collected when creating a connection. Set only when `auth_types` contains `oauth` or `user_oauth_app`.
---@field credential_parameters? digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryCredentialParametersList Non-secret values collected when registering an API key provider credential. They are validated against the provider's declaration and used to derive the credential's `base_url`; callers cannot supply header names or arbitrary destinations.
---@field oauth_redirect_url? string Callback URL a team must register with the provider when it creates its own OAuth client. It is the same for every provider and cannot be changed per credential. Empty unless `auth_types` contains `user_oauth_app`.
---@field oauth_client_setup_url? string HTTPS page at the provider where a team creates that OAuth client, such as its developer console or setup guide. Empty unless `auth_types` contains `user_oauth_app` and the provider declares one.

---Credential kinds the provider accepts, sorted:
---none|oauth|`shared_api_key`|unknown|`user_oauth_app`|`user_token`.
---
---`none` means the provider needs no credential. `oauth` means users can connect through
---DigitalOcean's shared OAuth application. `user_oauth_app` means users can connect through an OAuth
---client your team registers as a provider credential; without `oauth` alongside it, that is the only
---way to connect. `shared_api_key` means DigitalOcean supplies the key. `user_token` means your team
---or its users supply a key or token.
---
---`unknown` means the provider declares no kind this API recognizes, including an OAuth provider whose
---shared application is not available. It is never paired with another kind.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryAuthTypesList string[]

---Non-sensitive values collected when creating a connection. Set only when `auth_types` contains `oauth` or `user_oauth_app`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryConnectionParametersList digitalocean.digitalocean.ConnectionParameterSpec[]

---Non-secret values collected when registering an API key provider credential. They are validated against the provider's declaration and used to derive the credential's `base_url`; callers cannot supply header names or arbitrary destinations.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryCredentialParametersList digitalocean.digitalocean.ConnectionParameterSpec[]

---The OAuth scopes a connection may request; a connection that requests none gets all of them. Set only when `auth_types` contains `oauth` or `user_oauth_app`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderSummaryScopesList string[]

