---Validation outcome for one resolved rule.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdict
---@field rule? digitalocean.digitalocean.ResolvedRule
---@field verdict? digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdictVerdict exact — enforced precisely as written; degraded — renderable only in a more-restrictive form (deny→ask), warned; unsupported — cannot be enforced (strict ⇒ session reject); unverified — no descriptor available, rendered conservatively but unproven.
---@field rendered? digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdictRendered The disposition the agent will actually enforce: the requested action when exact/unverified, the more-restrictive target when degraded, omitted when unsupported (cannot render).
---@field reason? string Human-readable explanation of the verdict.
---@field suggestion? string Optional actionable hint (e.g. "set enforcement: best-effort, or target a capable agent").

---The disposition the agent will actually enforce: the requested action when exact/unverified, the more-restrictive target when degraded, omitted when unsupported (cannot render).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdictRendered "allow"|"ask"|"deny"

---exact — enforced precisely as written; degraded — renderable only in a more-restrictive form (deny→ask), warned; unsupported — cannot be enforced (strict ⇒ session reject); unverified — no descriptor available, rendered conservatively but unproven.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdictVerdict "exact"|"degraded"|"unsupported"|"unverified"

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.RunGatewayCodeRequest
---@field xSessionId? string The session to act in: the UUID at the end of the session's `sessionUrn` and `mcpUrl`. For a pinned endpoint version, use the session UUID at the end of its `mcp_url`, not the composite version ID. The session must belong to the authenticated user and team. Send either this header or `X-Endpoint-Id`, not both; both returns 400. With neither, the request uses your default endpoint when default endpoints are enabled for your team, and otherwise returns 403.
---@field xEndpointId? string The endpoint to act in, as a lowercase endpoint UUID. The request uses the endpoint's current head version, which the response reports in `X-Action-Gateway-Endpoint-Version`. The endpoint must belong to the authenticated user and team; an unknown or inaccessible endpoint returns 404. Send either this header or `X-Session-Id`, not both. A malformed value or more than one value returns 400.
---@field xActorId? string The actor you expect the session or endpoint to be bound to. It does not select an actor or connections; those come from the session's or endpoint's `actor_id`. When sent, it must equal that binding. A different value, including any value for a target with no actor, returns 403 with the message "The session is not bound to the request's actor."
---@field code string Python source to run. The sandbox provides `invoke_digitalocean_tool(name: str, arguments: dict) -> dict`, which calls a catalog tool under the session's policy and returns a tool result.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.RunGatewayCodeResponse
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.RunGatewayCodeResponseStatus
---@field output? digitalocean.digitalocean.RunGatewayCodeResponseOutput The tool's JSON output. Present when `status` is `succeeded`. Its shape is the tool's output schema, or the output view bound to the tool in the session.
---@field error? digitalocean.digitalocean.ErrorEnvelope
---@field call_id string A unique identifier for this call. Include it when contacting support.
---@field _meta? digitalocean.digitalocean.RunGatewayCodeResponseMeta Additional result metadata. Keys include: - `status`: `requires_approval`, `requires_authorization`, or `requires_connection_configuration` when the call stopped before running. - `approval_id`, `tool_name`, `expires_at`, and `decide`: present with `requires_approval`. `decide` gives the `method`, `path`, and `body` of the approval request to send. Approve the call, then repeat it with the same arguments before `expires_at`. - `retry`: `{"attempt_count": N, "exhausted": bool}` when the gateway retried the call. - `output_view`: the output view applied to the result. - `cache`: whether the result came from cache, with its age on a hit.

