---The result of one tool call. Check `status` before reading `output`. A call that needs approval, authorization, or connection setup fails with a `_meta.status` that names the step to complete.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResult
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultStatus
---@field output? digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultOutputMap The tool's JSON output. Present when `status` is `succeeded`. Its shape is the tool's output schema, or the output view bound to the tool in the session.
---@field error? digitalocean.digitalocean.ErrorEnvelope
---@field call_id string A unique identifier for this call. Include it when contacting support.
---@field _meta? digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultMeta Additional result metadata. Keys include: - `status`: `requires_approval`, `requires_authorization`, or `requires_connection_configuration` when the call stopped before running. - `approval_id`, `tool_name`, `expires_at`, and `decide`: present with `requires_approval`. `decide` gives the `method`, `path`, and `body` of the approval request to send. Approve the call, then repeat it with the same arguments before `expires_at`. - `retry`: `{"attempt_count": N, "exhausted": bool}` when the gateway retried the call. - `output_view`: the output view applied to the result. - `cache`: whether the result came from cache, with its age on a hit.

---A failed request. The body has the same shape as a failed tool result.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultError
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultErrorStatus
---@field error digitalocean.digitalocean.ErrorEnvelope
---@field call_id string A unique identifier for this request, when one was assigned.

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ToolResultErrorStatus "failed"

