---A reference to a span field, used in filters and `order_by`.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesFieldRef
---@field name string The field name. Without `scope`, these names (case-insensitive) resolve to built-in span columns: `trace_id`, `span_id`, `parent_span_id`, `start_time`, `end_time`, `duration_ns`, `name` (`span.name`), `kind` (`span.kind`), `status_code` (`status.code`, `status_code`), `status_message`, and `service_name` (`service.name`). Any other name is looked up as a span attribute, falling back to a resource attribute. With `scope` set, `name` is always treated as an attribute key. Attribute keys may contain only letters, digits, and `.`, `_`, `-`, `/`, `:`, `@`. In traces `order_by`, `name` must be a trace-level sort field instead; see the `order_by` field description.
---@field scope? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesFieldRefScope|string Restricts the lookup to one attribute map and is matched case-insensitively. `FIELD_SCOPE_RESOURCE` reads resource attributes and accepts `resource` or `resource.attributes` as aliases. `FIELD_SCOPE_ATTRIBUTES` reads span attributes and accepts `attribute`, `attributes`, or `span.attributes` as aliases. Omit to use the built-in column mapping described for `name`. Ignored in traces `order_by`.

---Restricts the lookup to one attribute map and is matched case-insensitively. `FIELD_SCOPE_RESOURCE` reads resource attributes and accepts `resource` or `resource.attributes` as aliases. `FIELD_SCOPE_ATTRIBUTES` reads span attributes and accepts `attribute`, `attributes`, or `span.attributes` as aliases. Omit to use the built-in column mapping described for `name`. Ignored in traces `order_by`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesFieldRefScope "FIELD_SCOPE_RESOURCE"|"FIELD_SCOPE_ATTRIBUTES"|"resource"|"resource.attributes"|"attribute"|"attributes"|"span.attributes"

---A sort clause for traces search results. Supported `field.name` values are `started`, `duration_ns`, `service_name`, `trace_id`, `error_count`, `span_count`, and `status`. Any other name returns `400`.
---
---Sorting by `started` is exact. For every other field, the server first selects the most recent matching traces by start time (up to the requested limit) and then sorts only those traces, so results are not a global top-N across the whole time range.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesOrderBy
---@field field digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesFieldRef
---@field direction? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesOrderByDirection|string The sort direction, matched case-insensitively. Omit to use the server default.

---The sort direction, matched case-insensitively. Omit to use the server default.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesOrderByDirection "asc"|"desc"

---Limits the size of a traces search result set. There is no cursor; use `pagination.has_more` in the response to tell whether more traces matched, and narrow the time range or filter to see them.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesPaginationRequest
---@field limit? number Maximum number of traces to return. Omitted or `0` uses the default of 100. Negative values or values above 1000 return `400`; they are not clamped.

---Pagination response.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesPaginationResponse
---@field has_more boolean Whether more results matched the query than were returned.

---Response body for a traces search.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSearchResponse
---@field data digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSearchResponseDataList Matching traces. Empty when no traces match.
---@field pagination digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesPaginationResponse

---Matching traces. Empty when no traces match.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSearchResponseDataList digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummary[]

---A single span belonging to a trace.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecord
---@field trace_id string The trace this span belongs to.
---@field span_id string The span identifier.
---@field parent_span_id? string The parent span identifier. Omitted for the root span.
---@field start_time? string The span start time.
---@field end_time? string The span end time.
---@field duration_ns? number Span duration in nanoseconds.
---@field name? string The span name, typically the operation being performed.
---@field kind? string The OpenTelemetry span kind as a string, for example `Server`, `Client`, or `Internal`.
---@field status_code? string The OpenTelemetry span status code as a string: `Unset`, `Ok`, or `Error`.
---@field status_message? string The status description. Omitted when empty.
---@field service_name? string The service that emitted the span. Omitted when the span has no service.name resource attribute.
---@field resource? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecordResourceMap Resource attributes associated with the span.
---@field attributes? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecordAttributesMap Span attributes. Omitted when empty.

---Span attributes. Omitted when empty.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecordAttributesMap { [string]: string }

---Resource attributes associated with the span.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecordResourceMap { [string]: string }

---A single point in time. Set `absolute` or `relative`; if both are set, `absolute` is used.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTimeInstant
---@field absolute? string An absolute timestamp, either RFC3339 (with optional fractional seconds) or a Unix epoch integer as a decimal string. Epoch precision is inferred from magnitude: seconds, milliseconds, microseconds, or nanoseconds.
---@field relative? string A time relative to now. Use `now` for the current time, a bare duration such as `15m` or `24h` to look back from now, or an offset such as `now-2h` or `now+30m`. Supported units are `s`, `m`, `h`, `d`, and `w`; decimal amounts such as `1.5h` are allowed.

---An inclusive query time window. Both bounds are required, `from` must not be after `to`, and the window must not exceed 7 days (`168h`).
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTimeRange
---@field from digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTimeInstant
---@field to digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTimeInstant

---A single trace and all of its spans.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceResponse
---@field trace_id? string The trace identifier.
---@field spans? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceResponseSpansList Every span in the trace, ordered by start time.
---@field truncated? boolean True when the trace has more spans than were returned in this response. Omitted when false.

---Every span in the trace, ordered by start time.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceResponseSpansList digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesSpanRecord[]

---A single trace returned by a traces search. One row per trace, aggregated from its spans. Every field except `trace_id` is omitted when it holds its zero value (for example, `error_count` is absent when no spans errored).
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummary
---@field trace_id string The trace identifier.
---@field started? string The start time of the earliest span in the trace, in RFC 3339 format.
---@field service_name? string The service that emitted the root span. Omitted when the root span has no service.name resource attribute.
---@field duration_ns? number Wall-clock duration of the trace in nanoseconds.
---@field span_count? number The number of spans in the trace.
---@field error_count? number The number of spans in the trace with an `Error` status code. Omitted when zero.
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummaryStatus The rolled-up status of the trace. `Error` if any span has an `Error` status code, otherwise `Ok`.
---@field span_names? digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummarySpanNamesList The distinct span names present in the trace.

---The distinct span names present in the trace.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummarySpanNamesList string[]

---The rolled-up status of the trace. `Error` if any span has an `Error` status code, otherwise `Ok`.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TracesTraceSummaryStatus "Ok"|"Error"

---A single automation bound to exactly one agent/session (agent == session in v1). The nested block present depends on `kind` (webhook xor cron) and `session_mode` (fresh => session_template; reuse => bound_session_id). `agent_kind` is read-only and derived; the webhook secret, the output email address / Slack webhook URL, and any env values inside session_template are write-only and never returned.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Trigger
---@field trigger_id string Server-allocated UUID; opaque to clients.
---@field kind digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerKind
---@field name string Unique per team among non-deleted triggers. Same rules as session names; not UUID-form.
---@field status digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerStatus
---@field session_mode? digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerSessionMode
---@field agent_kind? digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentKind
---@field prompt_template? string The prompt sent on each fire. Opaque to clients; payload-interpolation syntax is server-defined. For cron triggers it must not reference payload placeholders.
---@field output? digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputRead
---@field session_template? string Present iff session_mode=fresh. The agents.yaml Agent manifest used to CREATE a session on each fire, returned with its env values REDACTED.
---@field bound_session_id? string Present iff session_mode=reuse. UUID of the existing PAUSED session this trigger resumes; may be shared by multiple triggers.
---@field webhook? digitalocean.digitalocean.WebhookConfig
---@field cron? digitalocean.digitalocean.CronConfig
---@field created_at? string
---@field updated_at? string

---One row per firing (webhook delivery or cron tick).
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerExecution
---@field execution_id? string
---@field trigger_id? string
---@field status? digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerExecutionStatus
---@field session_id? string The run's session. Populated once the session is created (fresh) or is known (reuse); empty before then.
---@field run_id? string Populated once SendInput acks; correlation/audit only. May be empty.
---@field failure_reason? string Client-safe reason when status=failed; absent otherwise. One of a fixed set of messages; do not parse it or match on substrings. Quote the execution_id when contacting support.
---@field created_at? string
---@field updated_at? string
---@field payload? string The raw webhook body or cron tick metadata. Returned by GetTriggerExecution only; omitted from list items. Cleared for terminal executions after the payload retention window (default 7 days from creation).
---@field output_text? string The doctl-parity transcript rendered from the run's SPI events. Returned by GetTriggerExecution only; omitted from list items.
---@field output_truncated? boolean True when output_text is incomplete. Returned by GetTriggerExecution only; omitted from list items.

---Per-firing outcome.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerExecutionStatus "pending"|"running"|"succeeded"|"failed"

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerInfo
---@field namespace string A unique string format of UUID with a prefix fn-.
---@field name string The trigger's unique name within the namespace.
---@field ["function"] string Name of function(action) that exists in the given namespace.
---@field type string String which indicates the type of trigger source like SCHEDULED.
---@field is_enabled boolean Indicates weather the trigger is paused or unpaused.
---@field created_at? string UTC time string.
---@field updated_at? string UTC time string.
---@field scheduled_details? digitalocean.digitalocean.ScheduledDetails
---@field scheduled_runs? digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerInfoScheduledRuns

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerInfoScheduledRuns
---@field last_run_at? string|distilled.Null Indicates last run time. null value indicates trigger not run yet.
---@field next_run_at? string|distilled.Null Indicates next run time. null value indicates trigger will not run.

---How the trigger fires - on an event (webhook) or on a schedule (cron). Immutable after create.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerKind "webhook"|"cron"

---none = nothing pushed; the result stays in run history for self-serve. email = the collected run output is emailed to a configured address. slack = the collected run output is posted to a Slack incoming webhook URL (channel fixed by the webhook at install time).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputMode "none"|"email"|"slack"

---Output-delivery configuration as seen on reads. The email address and Slack webhook URL are write-only and never returned.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputRead
---@field mode? digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputMode
---@field email_configured? boolean True when an email address is stored (mode=email).
---@field slack_configured? boolean True when a Slack incoming webhook URL is stored (mode=slack).

---Output-delivery configuration on create/update. Exactly one of email / slack is required for the matching mode and forbidden otherwise; destinations are stored encrypted and never returned.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputWrite
---@field mode digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerOutputMode|string
---@field email? string Destination address; required iff mode=email.
---@field slack? digitalocean.digitalocean.SlackOutputWrite

---fresh = a new session is created from the trigger's spec on every firing and destroyed after. reuse = the trigger binds an existing PAUSED session, resumed on each firing and paused after; multiple triggers may bind one session.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerSessionMode "fresh"|"reuse"

---Trigger lifecycle state. Soft-deleted triggers are never returned (404).
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.TriggerStatus "active"|"paused"

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.UnassignTagResourcesRequest
---@field tag_id string The name of the tag. Tags may contain letters, numbers, colons, dashes, and underscores. There is a limit of 255 characters per tag.
