---Disposition the agent will actually enforce as the catch-all: equals defaultAction when exact; the more-restrictive degrade target (usually ask) when degraded.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidationResultDefaultActionRendered "allow"|"ask"|"deny"

---exact — agent can enforce the catch-all as written; degraded — agent cannot enforce the requested defaultAction (warn-only; shipped value unchanged); omitted when no descriptor was available to classify against.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidationResultDefaultActionVerdict "exact"|"degraded"|"unsupported"|"unverified"

---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidationResultVerdictsList digitalocean.digitalocean.RuleVerdict[]

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.ValkeyAdvancedConfig
---@field valkey_maxmemory_policy? digitalocean.digitalocean.EvictionPolicyModel|string
---@field valkey_pubsub_client_output_buffer_limit? number Set output buffer limit for pub / sub clients in MB. The value is the hard limit, the soft limit is 1/4 of the hard limit. When setting the limit, be mindful of the available memory in the selected service plan.
---@field valkey_number_of_databases? number Set number of valkey databases. Changing this will cause a restart of valkey service.
---@field valkey_io_threads? number Valkey IO thread count
---@field valkey_lfu_log_factor? number Counter logarithm factor for volatile-lfu and allkeys-lfu maxmemory-policies
---@field valkey_lfu_decay_time? number LFU maxmemory-policy counter decay time in minutes
---@field valkey_ssl? boolean Require SSL to access Valkey
---@field valkey_timeout? number Valkey idle connection timeout in seconds
---@field valkey_notify_keyspace_events? string Set notify-keyspace-events option. Requires at least `K` or `E` and accepts any combination of the following options. Setting the parameter to `""` disables notifications. - `K` &mdash; Keyspace events - `E` &mdash; Keyevent events - `g` &mdash; Generic commands (e.g. `DEL`, `EXPIRE`, `RENAME`, ...) - `$` &mdash; String commands - `l` &mdash; List commands - `s` &mdash; Set commands - `h` &mdash; Hash commands - `z` &mdash; Sorted set commands - `t` &mdash; Stream commands - `d` &mdash; Module key type events - `x` &mdash; Expired events - `e` &mdash; Evicted events - `m` &mdash; Key miss events - `n` &mdash; New key events - `A` &mdash; Alias for `"g$lshztxed"`
---@field valkey_persistence? digitalocean.digitalocean.ValkeyAdvancedConfigValkeyPersistence|string When persistence is 'rdb', Valkey does RDB dumps each 10 minutes if any key is changed. Also RDB dumps are done according to backup schedule for backup purposes. When persistence is 'off', no RDB dumps and backups are done, so data can be lost at any moment if service is restarted for any reason, or if service is powered off. Also service can't be forked.
---@field valkey_acl_channels_default? digitalocean.digitalocean.ValkeyAdvancedConfigValkeyAclChannelsDefault|string Determines default pub/sub channels' ACL for new users if ACL is not supplied. When this option is not defined, all_channels is assumed to keep backward compatibility. This option doesn't affect Valkey configuration acl-pubsub-default.
---@field frequent_snapshots? boolean Frequent RDB snapshots When enabled, Valkey will create frequent local RDB snapshots. When disabled, Valkey will only take RDB snapshots when a backup is created, based on the backup schedule. This setting is ignored when valkey_persistence is set to off.
---@field valkey_active_expire_effort? number Active expire effort Valkey reclaims expired keys both when accessed and in the background. The background process scans for expired keys to free memory. Increasing the active-expire-effort setting (default 1, max 10) uses more CPU to reclaim expired keys faster, reducing memory usage but potentially increasing latency.

---Determines default pub/sub channels' ACL for new users if ACL is not supplied. When this option is not defined, all_channels is assumed to keep backward compatibility. This option doesn't affect Valkey configuration acl-pubsub-default.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ValkeyAdvancedConfigValkeyAclChannelsDefault "allchannels"|"resetchannels"

---When persistence is 'rdb', Valkey does RDB dumps each 10 minutes if any key is changed. Also RDB dumps are done according to backup schedule for backup purposes. When persistence is 'off', no RDB dumps and backups are done, so data can be lost at any moment if service is restarted for any reason, or if service is powered off. Also service can't be forked.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.ValkeyAdvancedConfigValkeyPersistence "off"|"rdb"

