---A persistent workspace: a set of files with its own ID, mounted at `/workspace` in the one session it is attached to and kept when that session is removed.
---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.Workspace
---@field workspace_id string Assigned at create and never reused. Treat it as an opaque string.
---@field name? string Optional label. Not unique, and never accepted in place of workspace_id.
---@field state digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspaceState
---@field attached_session_id? string The session that holds the workspace. Absent when no session does.
---@field size_limit_gib number Size limit in GiB, fixed at create. It is a quota, so the filesystem total inside the session is slightly lower.
---@field bytes_used number Estimated used space in bytes as of the last save. It can differ from the usage seen inside the session.
---@field last_saved_at? string Time of the newest complete save. Absent until the first save.
---@field created_at string When the workspace was created.
---@field updated_at string When a user request last changed the workspace. Equal to created_at until then. Saves made by the platform do not change it.
---@field created_by string UUID of the user that created the workspace.
---@field updated_by string UUID of the user whose request last changed the workspace. Equal to created_by until then.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrl
---@field part_number? number
---@field upload_url? string Presigned PUT URL for this part. PUT the part bytes here directly.

---@class digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrls
---@field transfer_id? string
---@field part_urls? digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrlsPartUrlsList One presigned PUT URL per requested part number, in request order.
---@field expires_at? string Shared expiry for all URLs in this batch.

---One presigned PUT URL per requested part number, in request order.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrlsPartUrlsList digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrl[]

---Lifecycle state of a persistent workspace. `AVAILABLE`: ready to attach to a new session. `ATTACHING`: a session is being created with it. `ATTACHED`: a session is using it. `RELEASING`: the session was removed and the files are being saved. `FAILED`: the workspace could not be saved or created; it keeps its last successful save. `DELETING`: a delete is in progress. States may be added; treat an unknown value as unavailable.
---@alias digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspaceState "AVAILABLE"|"ATTACHING"|"ATTACHED"|"RELEASING"|"FAILED"|"DELETING"

