---Cancel the agent turn in flight.
---
---Stops the turn `POST /input` started. Pass `run_id` from that response to name the turn; an empty body cancels whichever turn is in flight. `outcome` is `acked` when the agent accepted the interrupt, `no_turn` when nothing addressable was running, and `unsupported` when this agent cannot be interrupted. A session that cannot take a cancel at all — paused, still starting, being destroyed, or with no active run — answers 409 instead of an `outcome`, so treat that as "nothing to cancel" rather than a fault. A team that is not enabled for turn cancel receives 403. A cancel starts nothing and is not blocked by the prepayment gate.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/cancel`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CancelHarnessSessionTurnRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CancelSessionTurnResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_harness_session_turn(input) end

---Cancel a staged workspace transfer.
---
---Aborts an in-flight transfer. Idempotent: cancelling an already-terminal transfer returns `aborted: false` with the current status. The request body is optional.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/workspace/transfers/{transfer_id}/cancel`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CancelHarnessSessionWorkspaceTransferRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspaceTransferCancelled? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_harness_session_workspace_transfer(input) end

---Cancel a Batch Inference Job
---
---Requests cancellation of a batch job. The job transitions to `cancelling` and, once in-flight requests drain, to `cancelled`. Jobs already in a terminal state (`completed`, `failed`, `expired`, `cancelled`) cannot be cancelled and return `409 Conflict`. Cancellation is also rejected with `409 Conflict` while the job has not yet been submitted to the upstream provider — there is nothing to cancel until the provider batch id is assigned.
---
---Partial results produced before cancellation remain available via `GET /v1/batches/{batch_id}/results`.
---
---`POST /v1/batches/{batch_id}/cancel`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CancelInferenceBatchRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.Batch? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:cancel_inference_batch(input) end

