---Create a New Droplet
---
---To create a new Droplet, send a POST request to `/v2/droplets` setting the
---required attributes.
---
---A Droplet will be created using the provided information. The response body
---will contain a JSON object with a key called `droplet`. The value will be an
---object containing the standard attributes for your new Droplet. The response
---code, 202 Accepted, does not indicate the success or failure of the operation,
---just that the request has been accepted for processing. The `actions` returned
---as part of the response's `links` object can be used to check the status
---of the Droplet create event.
---
---### Create Multiple Droplets
---
---Creating multiple Droplets is very similar to creating a single Droplet.
---Instead of sending `name` as a string, send `names` as an array of strings. A
---Droplet will be created for each name you send using the associated
---information. Up to ten Droplets may be created this way at a time.
---
---Rather than returning a single Droplet, the response body will contain a JSON
---array with a key called `droplets`. This will be set to an array of JSON
---objects, each of which will contain the standard Droplet attributes. The
---response code, 202 Accepted, does not indicate the success or failure of any
---operation, just that the request has been accepted for processing. The array
---of `actions` returned as part of the response's `links` object can be used to
---check the status of each individual Droplet create event.
---
---`POST /v2/droplets`
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateDropletRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateDropletResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_droplet(input) end

---Create an Endpoint
---
---Creates a named endpoint and its first immutable version atomically. The MCP URL follows the highest-numbered live version; version_mcp_url stays pinned. The top-level insights field sets the endpoint's Insights consent; version.insights is deprecated and ignored. An invalid name returns 400 invalid_endpoint_name; a duplicate team name returns 409 endpoint_name_taken.
---
---`POST /v2/action-gateway/endpoints`
---Errors: BadRequest, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateEndpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointPublishResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_endpoint(input) end

---Create an Endpoint Version
---
---Publishes a new immutable version as the endpoint's head. Only the endpoint owner may create versions, and the actor binding must match the endpoint. An identity mismatch returns 404 endpoint_identity_mismatch. Inaccessible endpoints return 404 endpoint_not_found. Publishing identical contents still creates a new version identity and number; it never resurrects a deleted version. Versions carry no Insights consent: a request's insights field is deprecated and ignored, and the endpoint's consent applies to the new version. Neither new-version creation nor head replacement changes that consent; change it with PATCH /v2/action-gateway/endpoints/{endpoint_id}.
---
---`POST /v2/action-gateway/endpoints/{endpoint_id}/versions`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateEndpointVersionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointPublishResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_endpoint_version(input) end

---Promote an Endpoint Version
---
---Copies a live version's configuration into a new, higher-numbered head version and sets promoted_from_version_number. Existing versions never change. Only the endpoint owner may promote. An inaccessible endpoint returns 404 endpoint_not_found, and a deleted, unknown, or different endpoint's version returns 404 endpoint_version_not_found. The new version always has a new identity and number, even for identical contents; deleted identities are never resurrected. Head replacement does not change the endpoint's Insights consent, which applies to every version.
---
---`POST /v2/action-gateway/endpoints/{endpoint_id}/versions:promote`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateEndpointVersionPromotionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.EndpointPublishResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_endpoint_version_promotion(input) end

