---Create an Environment Config (environment spec + optional Insights opt-in).
---
---Accepts name, environment-spec YAML text, and optional Insights telemetry opt-in. Tenant secrets are declared inside the environment spec (write-only values), not as sibling request fields. Responses never echo secret values; GET/create may include credential slot metadata (name/source/provider only). Configs are immutable after create.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/configs`
---Errors: BadRequest, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessConfigRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentConfigResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_config(input) end

---Create a provider connection for one actor.
---
---Creates the connection `{provider}` will use for `user_id`. `user_id` is the actor identifier the connection acts for, not a DigitalOcean user id. Each actor has at most one active, pending, or expired connection per provider. If `user_id` already has one, the request fails with `409`. Find that connection's id with `GET /v2/agents/auth/{provider}/connections?user_id=...`, then resume or restart it with `POST /v2/agents/auth/{provider}/connections/{connection_id}/reconnect`, which keeps its scopes. Revoked connections do not count toward the limit, and list responses omit them. If the only connection `user_id` has for `{provider}` is revoked, for example by `DELETE`, create starts it again under the same connection id, with the scopes in this request. To change a connection's scopes, delete it and then create it. A successful create returns the connection as `pending`, with an `authorization` object for the interactive step. No token is returned. `github` is the provider served today.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/auth/{provider}/connections`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessProviderConnectionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderConnectionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_provider_connection(input) end

---CreateSession provisions a sandbox and starts a Harness Runtime session.
---
---Returns once the session row is allocated. Sandbox boot completes asynchronously.
---
---Two mutually exclusive request forms are selected by Content-Type (same contract as
---harness-api `harness.swagger.json`):
---- YAML (`application/x-yaml`, `application/yaml`, `text/yaml`, `text/x-yaml`): the environment
---  spec. Two environment-spec formats are accepted during the dual-format transition: the flat
---  format (primary) and the legacy `agents.digitalocean.com/v1alpha1` envelope (deprecated). A
---  top-level `apiVersion` key selects the legacy parser; its absence selects flat. Internally
---  persists a durable Environment Config, then creates the session.
---- JSON (`application/json`): `{name, config_id}` loads the config, resolves its credentials from
---  Secrets Manager at the version pinned when the config was created, and creates the session.
---
---The OpenAPI `requestBody` schemas the JSON form for client generation (Autorest cannot emit a
---multi–content-type body). The live API still accepts the YAML forms listed above.
---
---Successful responses may include `config_id` on the session. `X-Device-UUID` (if present) is
---persisted on the session row. Query parameters `openai_session_id` and `resume_on_topoff` apply to
---both forms; when both the JSON body field and `?resume_on_topoff=` are present, the query
---parameter wins.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsCreateSessionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_session(input) end

---CreateCheckpoint captures the session's live sandbox state as a durable checkpoint.
---
---Synchronous: blocks until the capture reaches READY and returns the terminal Checkpoint — clients never see PENDING on this endpoint and need no poll loop. The checkpoint binds the machine-state capture to the event-log cursor at the cut, so it can later seed forks (POST .../fork) and rollback. Checkpoints are taken between turns; a session with an active turn in flight returns 409. A checkpoint captures machine state only: the files of a persistent workspace the session has are not in it, and are saved by the workspace itself.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/checkpoints`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionCheckpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateCheckpointResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_session_checkpoint(input) end

---ForkSession creates child sessions from a checkpoint of this session.
---
---Each child boots a fresh sandbox from the checkpoint's machine-state capture and is drivable exactly like any other session (input, HITL), with parent_session_id and fork_id set for lineage. When from_checkpoint_id is omitted, an implicit checkpoint of the session "now" is captured first and the children fork from that. All-or-nothing: on failure nothing is left running.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/fork`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionForkRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ForkSessionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_session_fork(input) end

---SendInput delivers a user chat message into the session.
---
---The agent observes it on its next turn and emits subsequent events via StreamSession. The input is forwarded to the owning microVM's OHR inbound surface, which attributes it to a run and returns the run id.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/input`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionInputRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.SendInputResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_session_input(input) end

---Start a staged (large-file) workspace transfer.
---
---Creates an asynchronous, object-storage-backed transfer for payloads larger than the streaming path supports (> ~50 MiB). Bulk bytes never traverse harness-api: the client PUTs/GETs presigned DO Spaces URLs directly.
---
---Set `direction` to `upload` or `download`.
---- `upload`: responds 201 with `transfer_id` + `part_size`; the client then requests per-part presigned PUT URLs, uploads them to Spaces, and calls `commit`.
---- `download`: responds 202 with `transfer_id`; the client polls GET until `completed` and then fetches `download_url` from Spaces.
---
---Upload, download, and cancel are live.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/workspace/transfers`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessSessionWorkspaceTransferRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspaceTransferCreated? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_session_workspace_transfer(input) end

---CreateTemplate creates a team custom template and kicks a build.
---
---Creates a team-owned template from a customer OCI ref rebased onto a base template. team_id is stamped from the authenticated principal.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/templates`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessTemplateRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateTemplateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_template(input) end

---Create a persistent workspace.
---
---Creates a persistent workspace with a fixed size limit. A workspace is a set of files with its own ID that is mounted at `/workspace` in the session it is attached to, and is kept when that session is removed. Attach it to a session by passing `workspace_id` when you create the session from an Environment Config. A new workspace returns `201`. A retry with the same `Idempotency-Key` and body within 24 hours returns the existing workspace with `200`. Persistent workspaces are in public preview, free during public preview, and enabled per team; for a team without access this returns `403`.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/workspaces`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateHarnessWorkspaceRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateWorkspaceResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_harness_workspace(input) end

