---Create an Alert Rule
---
---To create an alert rule, send a POST request to `/v2/insights/alert-rules`
---with a `spec` containing `name`, `query`, `thresholds`, and at least one
---`notification_channels` binding. `status` defaults to
---`ALERT_RULE_STATUS_ACTIVE` when omitted. `re_alert_duration` defaults to
---`RE_ALERT_DURATION_4H` when omitted.
---
---`query.metric` must be a dotted OpenTelemetry name such as
---`do.droplets.cpu_utilization`. Underscored Prometheus-style names are
---rejected with `422 Unprocessable Entity`.
---
---`POST /v2/insights/alert-rules`
---Errors: BadRequest, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateInsightAlertRuleRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateInsightAlertRuleResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_insight_alert_rule(input) end

---Create a Dashboard
---
---To create a dashboard, send a POST request to `/v2/insights/dashboards`
---with a `spec` containing the dashboard definition as a JSON document
---serialized to a string.
---
---The server derives the dashboard's `name` and `description` from
---`spec.display.name` and `spec.display.description`. Dashboard names are
---unique within a team; reusing a name returns `409`.
---
---The response status is `200` and the body contains the created dashboard.
---
---`POST /v2/insights/dashboards`
---Errors: BadRequest, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateInsightDashboardRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateInsightDashboardResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_insight_dashboard(input) end

---Create a Notification Channel
---
---To create a notification channel, send a POST request to
---`/v2/insights/notification-channels` with a `name` and exactly one of
---`email`, `slack`, or `webhook`.
---
---Email recipients must be team contact emails added and verified by a team
---owner. Webhook URLs must
---use HTTPS. Secret fields (`slack.webhook_url`, webhook credentials) are
---write-only. Subsequent reads never return secret values; they include
---optional `*_status` objects when a secret is configured.
---
---`POST /v2/insights/notification-channels`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateInsightNotificationChannelRequest
