---Register an MCP Server
---
---Registers a remote MCP server for your team, using the streamable HTTP transport. The server starts with `syncStatus` pending and no tools: discover its tools with `POST .../mcp-servers/{server_ref}/resync`, then choose which to enable with `PUT .../mcp-servers/{server_ref}/tools`. The endpoint must be HTTPS and resolve only to public IP addresses. The number of servers per team is limited (10 by default); registering beyond it returns 429. Returns 409 when `serverRef` is already in use.
---
---`POST /v2/action-gateway/mcp-servers`
---Errors: BadRequest, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMcpServerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_mcp_server(input) end

---Create a MicroVM
---
---To create a MicroVM, send a POST request to `/v2/microvms`.
---
---`name` and `source` are required. Set `source.oci_ref` to create the MicroVM from a
---`linux/amd64` container image, or `source.checkpoint_id` to create it from a checkpoint.
---With `oci_ref`, `region` and `size` are also required.
---
---A MicroVM created from an image is returned with `state` set to `creating`. Poll
---`GET /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}` until `state` is `running`. A MicroVM created from a
---checkpoint is usually returned already `running`.
---
---All settings are fixed at creation. There is no update endpoint.
---
---`POST /v2/microvms`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_microvm(input) end

---Create an access token for a MicroVM
---
---To create an API token that grants access to the public endpoint of one
---MicroVM only, send a POST request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/access_tokens`.
---
---The token value is returned once, in this response. Save it; list never
---returns it. To recover a lost token, revoke it and create a new one.
---
---The token works on every URL of the MicroVM: the default URL and any extra
---URL added with POST `/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/urls`. This token does not
---restrict team tokens: team members with `microvm:access` keep their access
---to the MicroVM. A MicroVM can have at most 10 live access tokens. Deleting
---the MicroVM revokes its tokens.
---
---`POST /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/access_tokens`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmAccessTokenRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmAccessTokenResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_microvm_access_token(input) end

---Create a checkpoint of a MicroVM
---
---To create a checkpoint of a running or paused MicroVM, send a POST request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/checkpoints`.
---
---The capture runs in the background and does not change the MicroVM's state. Poll
---`GET /v2/microvms/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}` until `status` is `CHECKPOINT_AVAILABLE`.
---
---`POST /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/checkpoints`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmCheckpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmCheckpointResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_microvm_checkpoint(input) end

---Add a URL to a MicroVM
---
---To add a public URL to a MicroVM, send a POST request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/urls`.
---
---The URL routes to `port`, which must be one of the ports declared at create;
---the MicroVM's port set cannot change. The call returns once the URL is
---recorded; its `status` is `PENDING` until the route is published.
---
---The MicroVM must be running or paused. A MicroVM can have at most 10 URLs,
---the default one included.
---
---`POST /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/urls`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmURLRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateMicrovmURLResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_microvm_url(input) end

