---Delete an Endpoint
---
---Deletes an endpoint and all its versions. The owner or a team owner may delete it. Missing endpoints, endpoints outside your team, and otherwise invisible endpoints all return the same empty 204 response as a successful deletion. A service-managed endpoint is invisible: deleting its ID returns the same 204 as an unknown ID and does not change it. Repeating a delete returns 204. Deletion is final for the endpoint identity and all cascaded version identities; retries, replays, and later writes cannot resurrect them. Reusing the same contents requires a new endpoint identity and a new version identity and number.
---
---`DELETE /v2/action-gateway/endpoints/{endpoint_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteEndpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteEndpointResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_endpoint(input) end

---Delete an Endpoint Version
---
---Deletes a live version. Only the endpoint owner may delete versions. Deleting the head makes the highest-numbered remaining live version the head. With no live versions, the endpoint MCP URL fails closed until another version is published. Inaccessible or deleted versions return 404 endpoint_version_not_found, and so does a version of a service-managed endpoint, exactly as for an unknown ID. Deletion is final for the version identity. Retries, replays, and later writes cannot resurrect it. Reusing identical contents requires a new version identity and version number.
---
---`DELETE /v2/action-gateway/endpoint-versions/{version_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteEndpointVersionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteEndpointVersionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_endpoint_version(input) end

