---Delete a Kubernetes Cluster
---
---To delete a Kubernetes cluster and all services deployed to it, send a DELETE
---request to `/v2/kubernetes/clusters/$K8S_CLUSTER_ID`.
---
---A 204 status code with no body will be returned in response to a successful
---request.
---
---`DELETE /v2/kubernetes/clusters/{cluster_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesClusterRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesClusterResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_kubernetes_cluster(input) end

---Delete a Node in a Kubernetes Cluster
---
---To delete a single node in a pool, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/kubernetes/clusters/$K8S_CLUSTER_ID/node_pools/$NODE_POOL_ID/nodes/$NODE_ID`.
---
---Appending the `skip_drain=1` query parameter to the request causes node
---draining to be skipped. Omitting the query parameter or setting its value to
---`0` carries out draining prior to deletion.
---
---Appending the `replace=1` query parameter to the request causes the node to
---be replaced by a new one after deletion. Omitting the query parameter or
---setting its value to `0` deletes without replacement.
---
---`DELETE /v2/kubernetes/clusters/{cluster_id}/node_pools/{node_pool_id}/nodes/{node_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesNodeRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesNodeResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_kubernetes_node(input) end

---Delete a Node Pool in a Kubernetes Cluster
---
---To delete a node pool, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/kubernetes/clusters/$K8S_CLUSTER_ID/node_pools/$NODE_POOL_ID`.
---
---A 204 status code with no body will be returned in response to a successful
---request. Nodes in the pool will subsequently be drained and deleted.
---
---`DELETE /v2/kubernetes/clusters/{cluster_id}/node_pools/{node_pool_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesNodePoolRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteKubernetesNodePoolResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_kubernetes_node_pool(input) end

---Delete a Load Balancer
---
---To delete a load balancer instance, disassociating any Droplets assigned to it
---and removing it from your account, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/load_balancers/$LOAD_BALANCER_ID`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/load_balancers/{lb_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteLoadBalancerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteLoadBalancerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_load_balancer(input) end

---Delete a Global Load Balancer CDN Cache
---
---To delete a Global load balancer CDN cache, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/load_balancers/$LOAD_BALANCER_ID/cache`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/load_balancers/{lb_id}/cache`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteLoadBalancerCacheRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteLoadBalancerCacheResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_load_balancer_cache(input) end

---Delete an MCP Server
---
---Disables all of the server's tools, removes them from your team's catalog, and deletes the server. An `api_key` supplied at registration is deleted; a `credentialRef` you supplied is left untouched. For a server registered with `credentialRefSource` connection, every user connection made through its OAuth client is revoked. Returns the deleted server, or 404 when it does not exist.
---
---`DELETE /v2/action-gateway/mcp-servers/{server_ref}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMcpServerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.McpServerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_mcp_server(input) end

---Delete a MicroVM
---
---To delete a MicroVM and the data on its disk, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}`. The MicroVM's checkpoints are not deleted.
---
---A successful request returns a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_microvm(input) end

---Revoke an access token of a MicroVM
---
---To revoke an access token, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/access_tokens/{token_id}`. The token stops
---working at the edge right away and drops out of the list. Revoke is
---permanent; a revoked token cannot be restored.
---
---A successful request returns a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/access_tokens/{token_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmAccessTokenRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmAccessTokenResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_microvm_access_token(input) end

---Delete a checkpoint
---
---To delete a checkpoint, send a DELETE request to `/v2/microvms/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}`.
---You can no longer create MicroVMs from a deleted checkpoint.
---
---The request returns HTTP 400 while the checkpoint is still being captured. A successful
---request returns a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/microvms/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmCheckpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmCheckpointResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_microvm_checkpoint(input) end

---Remove a URL from a MicroVM
---
---To remove a public URL from a MicroVM, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/urls/{url_id}`. The URL stops serving traffic.
---The system default URL cannot be removed.
---
---A successful request returns a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/urls/{url_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmURLRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteMicrovmURLResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_microvm_url(input) end

