function Client:delete_monitoring_sink(input) end

---Delete an NFS share
---
---To delete an NFS share, send a DELETE request to `/v2/nfs/{nfs_id}?region=${region}`.
---
---A successful request will return a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/nfs/{nfs_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteNfsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteNfsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_nfs(input) end

---Delete an NFS access point
---
---To delete an NFS access point, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/nfs/access_points/{access_point_id}`.
---
---A successful request will soft-delete the access point and return the deleted access point
---with status `ACCESS_POINT_DELETED` and an action object indicating the delete operation.
---
---The default access point (`is_default: true`) cannot be deleted. Access points already
---in `ACCESS_POINT_DELETED` or `ACCESS_POINT_FAILED` status return `400 Bad Request`.
---
---`DELETE /v2/nfs/access_points/{access_point_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteNfsAccessPointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.AccessPointActionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_nfs_access_point(input) end

---Delete an NFS snapshot
---
---To delete an NFS snapshot, send a DELETE request to `/v2/nfs/snapshots/{nfs_snapshot_id}?region=${region}`.
---
---A successful request will return a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/nfs/snapshots/{nfs_snapshot_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteNfsSnapshotRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteNfsSnapshotResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_nfs_snapshot(input) end

---Delete an Output View
---
---Deletes one of your team's views and returns it with audit.deleted_at set; it can no longer be used. Published views cannot be deleted. Returns 404 when the view does not exist, is already deleted, or is not your team's.
---
---`DELETE /v2/action-gateway/output-views/{view_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteOutputViewRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.OutputViewResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_output_view(input) end

---Delete an existing partner attachment
---
---To delete an existing partner attachment, send a `DELETE` request to
---`/v2/partner_network_connect/attachments/{pa_id}`.
---
---`DELETE /v2/partner_network_connect/attachments/{pa_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeletePartnerAttachmentRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeletePartnerAttachmentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_partner_attachment(input) end

---Delete an Existing Project
---
---To delete a project, send a DELETE request to `/v2/projects/$PROJECT_ID`. To
---be deleted, a project must not have any resources assigned to it. Any existing
---resources must first be reassigned or destroyed, or you will receive a 412 error.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/projects/{project_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteProjectRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteProjectResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_project(input) end

---Delete a Provider Credential
---
---Deletes a provider credential and every connection that uses it. There is no
---confirmation step. Warn affected users before deleting; sessions relying on
---those connections lose provider access. To rotate a key without removing
---connections, update the credential instead.
---
---Returns the deleted credential with status `PROVIDER_CREDENTIAL_STATUS_DELETED`
---and the number of removed connections in `revoked_connections`. Returns 404 for
---an unknown or already-deleted credential. A credential still bound to an MCP
---server cannot be deleted separately; delete the server first.
---
---`DELETE /v2/action-gateway/provider-credentials/{id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteProviderCredentialsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ProviderCredentialResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_provider_credentials(input) end

---Delete Container Registry By Name
---
---To delete your container registry, destroying all container image data stored in it, send a DELETE request to `/v2/registries/{registry_name}`.
---
---`DELETE /v2/registries/{registry_name}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_registry(input) end

---Delete Container Registry Repository
---
---To delete a container repository including all of its tags, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/registries/$REGISTRY_NAME/repositories/$REPOSITORY_NAME`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/registries/{registry_name}/repositories/{repository_name}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_registry_repository(input) end

---Delete Container Registry Repository Manifest
---
---To delete a container repository manifest by digest in one of your registries, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/registries/$REGISTRY_NAME/repositories/$REPOSITORY_NAME/digests/$MANIFEST_DIGEST`.
---
---Note that if your repository name contains `/` characters, it must be
---URL-encoded in the request URL. For example, to delete
---`registry.digitalocean.com/example/my/repo@sha256:abcd`, the path would be
---`/v2/registry/example/repositories/my%2Frepo/digests/sha256:abcd`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---It is similar to DELETE `/v2/registry/$REGISTRY_NAME/repositories/$REPOSITORY_NAME/digests/$MANIFEST_DIGEST`.
---
---`DELETE /v2/registries/{registry_name}/repositories/{repository_name}/digests/{manifest_digest}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryManifestRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryManifestResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_registry_repository_manifest(input) end

---Delete Container Registry Repository Tag
---
---To delete a container repository tag in on of our container registries, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/registries/$REGISTRY_NAME/repositories/$REPOSITORY_NAME/tags/$TAG`.
---
---Note that if your repository name contains `/` characters, it must be
---URL-encoded in the request URL. For example, to delete
---`registry.digitalocean.com/example/my/repo:mytag`, the path would be
---`/v2/registry/example/repositories/my%2Frepo/tags/mytag`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully. It is similar to DELETE `/v2/registry/$REGISTRY_NAME/repositories/$REPOSITORY_NAME/tags/$TAG`.
---
---`DELETE /v2/registries/{registry_name}/repositories/{repository_name}/tags/{repository_tag}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryTagRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteRegistryRepositoryTagResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_registry_repository_tag(input) end

---Delete a Reserved IP
---
---To delete a reserved IP and remove it from your account, send a DELETE request
---to `/v2/reserved_ips/$RESERVED_IP_ADDR`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/reserved_ips/{reserved_ip}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteReservedIPRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteReservedIPResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_reserved_ip(input) end

---Delete a Reserved IPv6
---
---To delete a reserved IP and remove it from your account, send a DELETE request
---to `/v2/reserved_ipv6/$RESERVED_IPV6`.
---
---A successful request will receive a 204 status code with no body in response.
---This indicates that the request was processed successfully.
---
---`DELETE /v2/reserved_ipv6/{reserved_ipv6}`
---Errors: NotFound, UnprocessableEntity.
