---Delete a Snapshot
---
---Both Droplet and volume snapshots are managed through the `/v2/snapshots/`
---endpoint. To delete a snapshot, send a DELETE request to
---`/v2/snapshots/$SNAPSHOT_ID`.
---
---A status of 204 will be given. This indicates that the request was processed
---successfully, but that no response body is needed.
---
---`DELETE /v2/snapshots/{snapshot_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSnapshotRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSnapshotResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_snapshot(input) end

---Delete a Snapshot Copy from a Region
---
---A Droplet snapshot that has been transferred to additional regions holds an
---independent copy in each one. To delete the copy in a single region without
---affecting the snapshot or its copies in other regions, send a DELETE request
---to `/v2/snapshots/$SNAPSHOT_ID/regions/$REGION`.
---
---The regions a snapshot holds copies in are listed in the `regions` attribute
---of the snapshot. The copy in the snapshot's original region cannot be
---deleted individually; to delete the snapshot entirely, use
---`DELETE /v2/snapshots/$SNAPSHOT_ID`. This endpoint is only available for
---Droplet snapshots.
---
---A status of 204 will be given. This indicates that the request was processed
---successfully, but that no response body is needed.
---
---`DELETE /v2/snapshots/{snapshot_id}/regions/{region}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSnapshotRegionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSnapshotRegionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_snapshot_region(input) end

---Delete a Spaces Access Key
---
---To delete a Spaces Access Key, send a DELETE request to `/v2/spaces/keys/$ACCESS_KEY`.
---
---A successful request will return a `204 No Content` status code.
---
---`DELETE /v2/spaces/keys/{access_key}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSpacesKeyRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSpacesKeyResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete_spaces_key(input) end

---Delete an SSH Key
---
---To destroy a public SSH key that you have in your account, send a DELETE request to `/v2/account/keys/$KEY_ID` or `/v2/account/keys/$KEY_FINGERPRINT`.
---A 204 status will be returned, indicating that the action was successful and that the response body is empty.
---
---`DELETE /v2/account/keys/{ssh_key_identifier}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.DeleteSshKeyRequest
