---Open a console in a MicroVM
---
---To open an interactive `/bin/sh` console in a MicroVM's workload container, open a
---WebSocket connection to `wss://api.digitalocean.com/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/console`.
---
---Send the API token in the `Authorization` header of the handshake. Browsers cannot set this
---header, so you cannot open the console from browser JavaScript. The image must include
---`/bin/sh`. A MicroVM can have four consoles open at a time. If the MicroVM is paused and
---auto-resume is on, opening a console resumes it.
---
---`GET /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/console`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.GetMicrovmConsoleRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.GetMicrovmConsoleResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_microvm_console(input) end

---Download a file from a MicroVM
---
---To read a file from a MicroVM's workload container, send a GET request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/files?path=<absolute path>`.
---
---The response body is the raw file content with a `Content-Type` of
---`application/octet-stream`. The `Content-Length` and `X-Checksum-Sha256` headers describe the
---file as it was when the transfer began. Only regular files of up to 64 MiB can be downloaded.
---A MicroVM serves up to 4 downloads at a time.
---
---Your team needs the `file_transfer` feature. Check `GET /v2/microvms/options`. If the MicroVM
---is paused and auto-resume is on, the request resumes it.
---
---`GET /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/files`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.GetMicrovmFileRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.GetMicrovmFileResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_microvm_file(input) end

---List MicroVM options
---
---To list the default region, sizes, prices, account limits, and features available to
---your team, send a GET request to `/v2/microvms/options`.
---
---`GET /v2/microvms/options`
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.GetMicrovmOptionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.MicrovmOptions? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_microvm_options(input) end

