---CancelExecution ends a running execution and frees the trigger's in-flight slot.
---
---Fails the execution and frees the trigger's in-flight slot. A fresh-mode session is destroyed outright. A reuse-mode session is only paused, not stopped - harness has no run-interrupt call, so the agent's turn may still be in flight server-side; this frees the queue, not necessarily the agent's work. A non-running execution is a no-op that still returns 200.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}/executions/{execution_id}/cancel`
---Errors: NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCancelTriggerExecutionRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.GetTriggerExecutionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_cancel_trigger_execution(input) end

---Clone an Environment Config under a new name.
---
---Copies the source config's sanitized manifest to a new UUID. Source and clone are independent (no lineage). Credential bindings are never copied: if the manifest declares secret slots, supply secrets/oauth_assignments again (write-only). content_hash matches the source when the manifest is unchanged.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/configs/{config_id}/clone`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCreateConfigCloneRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.AgentConfigResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_create_config_clone(input) end

---Start an interactive provider login for the team.
---
---Starts, or resumes, the one-time login the team uses so a session can act on a provider. `github` is the provider served today; any other value returns 501. The body is optional. When the team is already connected, `status` is `success` and no URL is returned. Otherwise `status` is `requires_authorization` and the response carries the URL, verification code, and poll URL for the interactive step. No token or authorization handle is returned.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/auth/{provider}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCreateProviderConnectRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.StartProviderConnectResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_create_provider_connect(input) end

---Mint presigned PUT URLs for one or more multipart upload parts.
---
---Upload only. Pass one or more 1-based `part_numbers`; the response returns a presigned `upload_url` per part (all sharing one `expires_at`), so a client can drive parallel part uploads without a round trip per part. PUT each part's bytes directly to its URL (bypassing harness-api). If URLs expire before the PUT, request them again.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/workspace/transfers/{transfer_id}/part-upload-urls`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCreateSessionWorkspacePartUploadUrlsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspacePartUploadUrls? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_create_session_workspace_part_upload_urls(input) end

---Upload a file or tar archive into the session's sandbox workspace.
---
---Streams the raw request body to a path inside the sandbox workspace. Concurrent transfers (upload + download) are capped server-side; over the cap the request blocks and may return 503. The optional `X-Content-Sha256` request header carries a hex digest the guest verifies after the full payload is written.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/workspace/upload`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCreateSessionWorkspaceUploadRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.WorkspaceUploadResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_create_session_workspace_upload(input) end

---CreateTrigger creates a webhook or cron trigger.
---
---Validation is synchronous, so a mistake is a 400/409 at creation, not a silent miss at the first
---fire. Exactly one of `webhook` / `cron` must be present and match `kind`. kind=cron forbids a
---`webhook` block and requires a parseable `cron.cron_expr` and a valid IANA `cron.timezone`.
---session_mode=fresh requires `session_template` (a well-formed agents.yaml Agent manifest) and
---forbids `bound_session_id`; session_mode=reuse requires `bound_session_id` (an existing team-owned
---session) and forbids `session_template`. `output.mode` selects the destination block (email/slack),
---which is stored encrypted. `name` must be unique per team among non-deleted triggers. Triggers do
---not support persistent workspaces: a `session_template` that names `workspace_id`, and a
---`bound_session_id` whose session has a workspace, are both refused.
---
---For webhook triggers the response includes `webhook_secret` exactly ONCE - it is never returned
---again. Cron triggers return no secret and carry a computed `trigger.cron.next_run_at`. The team and
---user identity are taken from the authenticated principal, never the body.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/triggers`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessCreateTriggerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.CreateTriggerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_create_trigger(input) end

---DeleteTrigger soft-deletes a trigger.
---
---Marks the trigger deleted, fails any pending executions, and purges the webhook secret / cron schedule. A fresh trigger owns no session; a reuse trigger only UNBINDS - it never destroys the customer's session. Execution history and by-session lookups continue to resolve to the deleted row. Returns 204 No Content on success.
---
---`DELETE /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessDeleteTriggerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessDeleteTriggerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_delete_trigger(input) end

---Check whether a provider login has finished.
---
---Pass the `poll_url` from the start response. The response reports only whether login has finished. No token or authorization handle is returned. `github` is the provider served today.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/auth/{provider}/poll`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessGetProviderConnectRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.PollProviderConnectResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_get_provider_connect(input) end

---Download a file or tar archive from the session's sandbox workspace.
---
---Streams the workspace payload back as `application/octet-stream` using chunked transfer encoding, followed by a fixed integrity footer.
---
---Response body layout: `<payload>` + `<footer>`, where the footer is exactly 73 bytes: `DOWSSHA1` (8 bytes) + 64-char lowercase SHA-256 hex + `\n`. The client MUST strip the trailing 73 bytes before saving, verify SHA-256(payload) equals the footer digest, and treat a tail that does not match this shape (magic + 64 hex + newline) as a failed (truncated/corrupt) transfer.
---
---Other metadata:
---- `X-Workspace-Is-Archive: true` when the payload is a tar archive.
---- `X-Workspace-Size-Bytes` is a progress hint (not Content-Length) and excludes the footer.
---- The `X-Content-Sha256` trailer also carries the digest but is best-effort: edge proxies may strip HTTP trailers, so the body footer is authoritative.
---
---Concurrent transfers (upload + download) are capped server-side; over the cap the request blocks and may return 503.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/workspace/download`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessGetSessionWorkspaceDownloadRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessGetSessionWorkspaceDownloadResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_get_session_workspace_download(input) end

---GetTrigger returns a single trigger by id.
---
---GetTrigger returns a single trigger by id. Write-only fields (webhook secret, output destination, session_template env values) are never included.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}`
