---`GET /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}/executions`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessListTriggerExecutionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ListTriggerExecutionsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_list_trigger_executions(input) end

---ResumeSession explicitly thaws a PAUSED session's microVM sandbox.
---
---Only valid for microvm-substrate sessions; dewdrop/docker sessions return 501 Not Implemented. Implicit resume also occurs when SendInput or ResolveHITL is called on a paused session. Returns synchronously once the sandbox is ready.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/resume`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessPostSessionResumeRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessPostSessionResumeResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_post_session_resume(input) end

---ExecInSandbox runs a one-shot command inside the session's sandbox.
---
---Runs `argv` directly in the guest (no shell). Stdout/stderr are buffered and capped at 1 MiB each;
---truncation is indicated via response headers when present. A non-zero exit code is still HTTP 200.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/sandbox/exec`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessPostSessionSandboxExecRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ExecInSandboxResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_post_session_sandbox_exec(input) end

---RotateTriggerSecret issues a new webhook secret.
---
---Webhook triggers only (409 for cron). Issues a new secret (shown once) and moves the old value to
---the previous slot, where it keeps verifying deliveries until previous_secret_expires_at. Default
---grace is 5 minutes when grace_period_seconds is omitted, so deliveries already in flight (signed
---with the old value) still succeed while the customer updates their external system. After that
---instant the old value is refused with 401. Pass grace_period_seconds=0 to retire the old secret on
---this call (breach response), or a positive value (up to the server max, default 1 hour) for a custom
---window; above the max is 400.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}/rotate-secret`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessPostTriggerRotateSecretRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.RotateSecretResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_post_trigger_rotate_secret(input) end

---ReceiveTriggerWebhook accepts a signed delivery from an external system.
---
---The one public, un-team-authenticated endpoint. There is NO DO bearer token: the caller is the
---customer's external system. Authentication is the per-trigger HMAC secret, verified on every
---delivery; edge rate-limiting is mandatory.
---
---The request body is the provider's RAW body, forwarded verbatim (the HMAC is computed over the exact
---bytes received); Content-Type is provider-defined and passed through. The signature header depends on
---the trigger's provider:
---  - github: `X-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=<hex>` (HMAC-SHA256 of the raw body)
---  - gitlab: `X-Gitlab-Token: <token>` (plaintext token equality; GitLab does not sign)
---  - custom: `X-DigitalOcean-Signature: t=<unix>,v1=<hex>` (HMAC-SHA256 of `{unix}.{raw body}`;
---    `do-signature` is also accepted as a transitional alias)
---
---On success (including a provider retry that dedupes to an existing firing) it returns 202 with the
---execution_id. A delivery to a paused trigger returns 202 with no body and queues nothing (deliberately
---not 409, so providers do not auto-disable the webhook after repeated non-2xx).
---
---`POST /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}/webhook`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessPostTriggerWebhookRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.WebhookAcceptedResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_post_trigger_webhook(input) end

---RollbackToCheckpoint rewinds a session to a checkpoint.
---
---In-place restore: boots a fresh sandbox from the checkpoint and atomically swaps the session's sandbox pointer to it, so the session keeps its same session_id; the old sandbox is then torn down.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/checkpoints/{checkpoint_id}/rollback`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessRevertSessionCheckpointRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.RollbackToCheckpointResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_revert_session_checkpoint(input) end

---UpdateTrigger updates, pauses, or re-enables a trigger.
---
---Partial update: only the supplied fields change. `kind` and `webhook.provider` are immutable
---(409 on change). Mutable: `name` (409 on duplicate), `status` (active<->paused), `prompt_template`,
---`output`, `session_template` (fresh), `bound_session_id` (reuse), `cron.cron_expr` /
---`cron.timezone` (recomputes next_run_at). Re-enabling never produces a catch-up run. PATCHing
---session_template is a full replacement, so every spec.secrets slot value the new manifest declares
---must be resupplied (secret values are never echoed back), or the request is a 400.
---
---`PATCH /v2/agents/triggers/{trigger_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessUpdateTriggerRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.GetTriggerResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:harness_update_trigger(input) end

---Accept an Image Account Transfer
---
---To accept an account transfer for an image, send a POST request to
---`/v2/images/$IMAGE_ID/account_transfer/accept`.
---
---`POST /v2/images/{image_id}/account_transfer/accept`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferAcceptRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferAcceptResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:images_post_account_transfer_accept(input) end

---Cancel an Image Account Transfer
---
---To cancel an account transfer for an image, send a POST request to
---`/v2/images/$IMAGE_ID/account_transfer/cancel`.
---
---Only the sender of an image account transfer can cancel the transfer.
---If the transfer is canceled, the image will remain in the sender's account
---and will not be transferred to the recipient.
---
---`POST /v2/images/{image_id}/account_transfer/cancel`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferCancelRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferCancelResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:images_post_account_transfer_cancel(input) end

---Initiate an Image Account Transfer
---
---To initiate an account transfer for an image, send a POST request to
---`/v2/images/$IMAGE_ID/account_transfer`.
---
---Only snapshot images may be transferred by this endpoint to another account.
---
---An image account transfer always has exactly one recipient, specified in the request body.
---The recipient can be one of the following:
---
---* A DigitalOcean account, denoted by `recipient_email` in the request body.
---The recipient will receive an email with instructions to accept the transfer.
---Once the recipient accepts the transfer, the image will be moved to their
---account.
---
---* A DigitalOcean team, denoted by `recipient_uuid` in the request body. If the
---user has sufficient permissions in the recipient team, the transfer will be
---automatically accepted and the image will be moved to the recipient team's
---account. Otherwise, the transfer will be pending until a user with sufficient
---permissions in the recipient team accepts the transfer.
---
---`POST /v2/images/{image_id}/account_transfer`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferCreateRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ImagesPostAccountTransferCreateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:images_post_account_transfer_create2(input) end

