---Returns the caller's sessions and checkpoints whose sandbox image carries a live notice. Pass `session_name` or `checkpoint_name` to look up one resource; those two parameters cannot be set together, and `page_size` / `page_token` are ignored when either is set. Without a name, the list is keyset-paginated. `type` filters the notice kind; the only documented value is `vulnerability`. Triggers are not listed here — a trigger runs on a session, so ask about that session.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/image-messages`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessImageMessagesRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ListImageMessagesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_image_messages(input) end

---List the team's connections for a provider.
---
---One page of connections the team holds for `{provider}`. `user_id` is the actor identifier the connection acts for, not a DigitalOcean user id. A list never includes revoked connections and never includes a token. `github` is the provider served today. Page defaults are the upstream connection service's own (20 per page, at most 100).
---
---`GET /v2/agents/auth/{provider}/connections`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessProviderConnectionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ListProviderConnectionsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_provider_connections(input) end

---ListRegions returns the regions the caller's team may create sessions and agent configs in.
---
---Per-team catalog the UI (and other clients) render as the region picker, instead of hardcoding the list. A region is chosen by the API host you call, not by a field in the request body, so a returned `slug` tells you which regional host to target — `ric1` means `https://api-ric1.digitalocean.com`. The default region is always listed and is marked `is_default`; its resources are also reachable on the region-less host, `https://api.digitalocean.com`. Every other open region is listed only when the team holds its placement grant, so a create on a listed region's host is admitted and a region missing from this list is refused. Teams not yet on the regional routing rollout see only the default region, and their responses carry no `region` field. Legacy regions are never listed. Sorted by slug; no pagination.
---
---`GET /v2/harness-runtime/regions`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessRegionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.HarnessRegionsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_regions(input) end

---ListReusableSessions lists the team's PAUSED sessions for the reuse picker.
---
---Returns the team's sessions in status PAUSED, for binding a session_mode=reuse trigger. The item shape is the hosted-agents Session, so `agent_kind` and `status` use the AGENT_KIND_* / SESSION_STATUS_* spelling; `status` is always SESSION_STATUS_PAUSED here.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/triggers/reusable-sessions`
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessReusableSessionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ListReusableSessionsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_reusable_sessions(input) end

---ListCheckpoints enumerates a session's checkpoints, newest first.
---
---Keyset-paginated on an opaque cursor, like ListSessions.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/sessions/{session_id}/checkpoints`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessSessionCheckpointsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ListCheckpointsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_session_checkpoints(input) end

---ListSandboxSizes returns the customer-selectable sandbox (microVM) size catalog.
---
---Read-only catalog the UI (and other clients) render as the size picker, instead of hardcoding the list. The set is the single source of truth shared with create-time validation and the default-size fallback, so every `slug` returned here is accepted by CreateSession as spec.sandbox.sizeSlug. Sizes are returned smallest-to-largest. Static and safe to cache; independent of team/session; no pagination.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/sessions/sandbox/sizes`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessSessionSandboxSizesRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.SandboxSizesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_session_sandbox_sizes(input) end

---ListSessions enumerates sessions for the caller's tenant.
---
---Keyset-paginated on an opaque cursor. Results are scoped to the authenticated team. Destroyed and failed sessions are omitted by default (matching the Cloud Console); pass `status=SESSION_STATUS_ALL` to list every session regardless of status, or an explicit status such as `status=SESSION_STATUS_FAILED` or `status=SESSION_STATUS_DESTROYED` to list only those.
---
---`GET /v2/agents/sessions`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ListHarnessSessionsRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.DefinitionsListSessionsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_harness_sessions(input) end

