---Decide a Pending Approval by Session Header
---
---Approves or denies a tool call that is waiting for approval, identifying the session with the `X-Session-Id` header or the endpoint with the `X-Endpoint-Id` header. With `X-Session-Id`, it behaves the same as `POST /approvals/session/{session_id}/{approval_id}`, which is the path returned in a result's `_meta.decide`. An unknown `X-Endpoint-Id` returns 404.
---
---`POST /approvals/{approval_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateGatewayApprovalRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ApprovalDecisionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_gateway_approval(input) end

---Decide a Pending Approval
---
---Approves or denies a tool call that is waiting for approval. A tool result returns `_meta.status` set to `requires_approval` when the session policy sets `ask` for the call, and its `_meta.decide` gives this request's path.
---
---Send the decision with the session owner's token. Approval is a separate control request, not a tool, so an agent cannot approve its own calls. After approving, repeat the original call with the same arguments before `expires_at`. An approval applies only to that session, tool version, and set of arguments, and is used once. To ask again after a denial or expiry, repeat the tool call.
---
---`POST /approvals/session/{session_id}/{approval_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateGatewaySessionApprovalRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ApprovalDecisionResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_gateway_session_approval(input) end

