---Update Consent for an Environment
---
---To enable or disable signals collection for a specific environment, send a
---PUT request to `/v1/consent/{environment_id}` with an `enabled` boolean in the
---request body.
---
---This endpoint only manages per-environment (`source: agent`) consent. To manage
---team-level consent for Serverless Inference, use
---`PUT /v1/consent?source=inference` instead.
---
---`PUT /v1/consent/{environment_id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateSignalConsentRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateSignalConsentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_signal_consent(input) end

---Update Team-Level Consent
---
---To enable or disable signals collection for a source that is consented at
---the team level, send a PUT request to `/v1/consent?source=inference` with
---an `enabled` boolean in the request body. Currently the only team-level
---source is `inference`, which covers Serverless Inference chat completions
---made by your team.
---
---To revoke consent, send the same request with `enabled` set to `false`.
---The `source` query parameter is required. Per-environment consent for Harness
---Runtime environments is managed with `PUT /v1/consent/{environment_id}` instead.
---
---`PUT /v1/consent`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateSignalTeamConsentRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.UpdateSignalTeamConsentResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_signal_team_consent(input) end

