---Upload a Batch Inference Input File
---
---Uploads the raw JSONL bytes to the presigned `upload_url` returned by `POST /v1/batches/files`.
---
---**The URL is dynamic — do not construct it.** Use the `upload_url` value from the previous step verbatim. Its host, path, and query parameters are part of the short-lived (~15 minute) signature and change per request; the server and path shown here are illustrative. If the URL expires before the upload completes, create a new file intent and retry.
---
---`POST /v1/batches` performs a `HEAD` check on the uploaded object and will reject the batch if this upload has not completed.
---
---Send the raw JSONL bytes verbatim. Presigned PUT URLs are signature-sensitive to request headers — prefer `application/octet-stream` or omit `Content-Type` entirely. A custom value (for example `application/jsonl`) can cause signature mismatches unless the URL was signed for that exact header.
---
---`PUT /<upload_url>`
---Errors: Forbidden.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.UploadInferenceBatchFileRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.UploadInferenceBatchFileResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:upload_inference_batch_file(input) end

---Upload a file to a MicroVM
---
---To write a file into a MicroVM's workload container, send a PUT request to
---`/v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/files?path=<absolute path>` with the raw file content as the
---request body and a `Content-Type` of `application/octet-stream`.
---
---The file replaces any existing regular file at `path` atomically. The parent directory
---must already exist. The request must carry a `Content-Length` header; chunked bodies are
---rejected. A body of up to 64 MiB is accepted, and a `Content-Length` of `0` writes an empty
---file. Pass `sha256` to have the API verify the content before it replaces the target.
---
---Your team needs the `file_transfer` feature. Check `GET /v2/microvms/options`. If the MicroVM
---is paused and auto-resume is on, the request resumes it.
---
---`PUT /v2/microvms/{microvm_id}/files`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.UploadMicrovmFileRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.FileInfo? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:upload_microvm_file(input) end

---Propose an App Spec
---
---To propose and validate a spec for a new or existing app, send a POST request to the `/v2/apps/propose` endpoint. The request returns some information about the proposed app, including app cost and upgrade cost. If an existing app ID is specified, the app spec is treated as a proposed update to the existing app.
---
---`POST /v2/apps/propose`
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidateAppAppSpecRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.AppProposeResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_app_app_spec(input) end

---Validate App Rollback
---
---Check whether an app can be rolled back to a specific deployment. This endpoint can also be used
---to check if there are any warnings or validation conditions that will cause the rollback to proceed
---under unideal circumstances. For example, if a component must be rebuilt as part of the rollback
---causing it to take longer than usual.
---
---`POST /v2/apps/{app_id}/rollback/validate`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidateAppRollbackRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidateAppRollbackResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_app_rollback(input) end

---ValidatePolicy checks a manifest's tool-permission policy against the agent's capabilities without creating a session.
---
---Stateless preflight: parses the same environment spec as CreateSession and runs the identical resolve + validate pipeline against the capability descriptor stamped on the selected template's image (resolved per-request via the sandbox, not a separate registry). Returns per-rule verdicts. Nothing is provisioned or persisted.
---
---Each rule is validated against the descriptor for the (agent, version) the template resolves to and gets a verdict: `exact`, `degraded`, `unsupported`, or `unverified`. `ok` is false when any strict rule is unsupported or unverified — i.e. CreateSession would reject the policy for that agent. An empty `spec.permissions` returns `ok: true` with no verdicts. Because it shares the create path's descriptor lookup, the verdicts match what CreateSession would compute.
---
---`POST /v2/agents/sessions/policy/validate`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input? digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidateHarnessSessionPolicyRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidationResult? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_harness_session_policy(input) end

---Preview an Output View
---
---Validates a projection exactly as create does and returns the view it would produce, including `output_schema`, without storing anything. name and description are optional here; name uniqueness and the per-tool-version limit are not checked.
---
---`POST /v2/action-gateway/output-views/preview`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input digitalocean.digitalocean.ValidateOutputViewRequest
---@return digitalocean.digitalocean.OutputViewResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:validate_output_view(input) end

